180	sqlserver	instruct	Choose resolution path based on infrastructure constraints	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "Three paths based on constraints:\\n\\nPATH A — Upgrade the DR/validation server (recommended): Install the same major version as the production source on the DR server. SQL Server backups are always restorable to the same or higher version. This is the only option that preserves full recoverability.\\n\\nPATH B — Use BACPAC export for schema+data portability (limited): Use SqlPackage.exe to export a BACPAC from the source: 'SqlPackage /Action:Export /SourceServerName:@source /SourceDatabaseName:@db /TargetFile:@db.bacpac'. Import on target: 'SqlPackage /Action:Import /TargetServerName:@target /TargetDatabaseName:@db /SourceFile:@db.bacpac'. Limitation: BACPAC does not preserve SQL Agent jobs, logins, linked servers, or certain T-SQL features.\\n\\nPATH C — Redirect validation backups to same-version server: If a same-version server is available, update the backup validation job to restore/verify on that server instead. Does not fix the DR gap but unblocks validation."}	null	low	f	t	5 days	2026-02-24 13:10:27.115336
181	sqlserver	instruct	Implement version matching policy for DR servers	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "Policy to prevent recurrence: (1) DR/validation servers must match or exceed the production SQL Server major version. (2) Before upgrading production SQL Server, upgrade DR servers first. (3) Include 'DR server version must be >= production version' as a go/no-go criterion in upgrade runbooks. (4) Add a weekly check: query msdb.dbo.backupset on the DR server for any backups with software_major_version > SERVERPROPERTY('ProductMajorVersion') and alert if any found."}	null	low	f	t	04:00:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.115337
