342	sqlserver	instruct	Establish memory sizing standard for all SQL Server instances	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "Prevent future memory overallocation: (1) Document the memory sizing formula: max_server_memory_MB = (total_RAM_GB * 1024) - OS_reservation_MB, where OS_reservation = max(10% of total RAM, 2048 MB). (2) Add max server memory validation to the server commissioning checklist. (3) For servers with other services (SSAS, SSRS, SSIS), reduce SQL Server memory further to accommodate co-located services. (4) Configure a SQL Agent alert on the Performance Monitor counter 'Memory Manager: Memory Grants Pending' > 0 to detect future memory pressure early. (5) Set 'max server memory' as a Policy-Based Management condition with the formula enforced automatically."}	null	low	f	t	02:00:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.11567
343	sqlserver	verify	Verify memory is stable and OS pressure is relieved	{"sql": "SELECT\\n  c.value_in_use AS max_server_memory_mb,\\n  si.physical_memory_kb / 1024 AS physical_memory_mb,\\n  CAST(c.value_in_use AS BIGINT) * 100 / (si.physical_memory_kb / 1024) AS pct_of_ram,\\n  sm.available_physical_memory_kb / 1024 AS os_available_mb,\\n  sm.system_memory_state_desc,\\n  pm.process_physical_memory_low,\\n  (SELECT cntr_value FROM sys.dm_os_performance_counters\\n   WHERE counter_name = 'Memory Grants Pending'\\n     AND object_name LIKE '%Memory Manager%') AS grants_pending\\nFROM sys.configurations c\\nCROSS JOIN sys.dm_os_sys_info si\\nCROSS JOIN sys.dm_os_sys_memory sm\\nCROSS JOIN sys.dm_os_process_memory pm\\nWHERE c.name = 'max server memory (MB)';", "parameters": [], "description": "Confirms max server memory is within safe bounds and OS memory pressure has been resolved."}	null	low	f	t	00:01:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.11567
