771	sqlserver	instruct	Update bulk load process to disable and rebuild indexes around the load	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "Optimal bulk load pattern for large datasets: (1) Before load: Disable non-clustered indexes (ALTER INDEX [nci_name] ON [table] DISABLE). (2) Run bulk load with TABLOCK hint and sorted data matching clustered index key order. (3) After load: Rebuild all indexes (ALTER INDEX ALL ON [table] REBUILD WITH (SORT_IN_TEMPDB=ON, MAXDOP=:n)). (4) Update statistics if not auto-updated. This pattern: eliminates mid-load fragmentation, allows SQL Server to use bulk load optimizations (minimal logging in simple/bulk-logged recovery), and produces a defragmented index after the rebuild. For incremental loads < 20% of table size, keep indexes enabled and accept fragmentation managed by nightly maintenance."}	null	low	f	t	5 days	2026-02-24 13:10:27.184966
