1085	sqlserver	instruct	Update connection string with correct timeout and routing parameters	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["listener_dns: DNS name from sys.availability_group_listeners", "port: Listener port (typically 1433)", "db: Target database name"], "description": "Update the health check probe connection string with the following recommended parameters:\\n\\n1. Set MultiSubnetFailover=True — required for AG listener to enable fast failover detection across subnets.\\n2. Set ConnectTimeout=15 (minimum; increase to 30 for cross-datacenter listeners) — prevents premature timeout failures.\\n3. Set ApplicationIntent=ReadWrite for primary-targeted health checks; use ApplicationIntent=ReadOnly only if intentionally routing to readable secondaries.\\n4. Set LoginTimeout=15 to align with ConnectTimeout.\\n5. Set Encrypt=True;TrustServerCertificate=True (or configure proper certificate) if SQL Server requires encrypted connections.\\n\\nExample corrected JDBC connection string:\\n  jdbc:sqlserver://<listener_dns>:<port>;databaseName=<db>;MultiSubnetFailover=True;ConnectTimeout=30;LoginTimeout=30;ApplicationIntent=ReadWrite;Encrypt=True;TrustServerCertificate=True\\n\\nFor .NET SqlClient:\\n  Server=<listener_dns>,<port>;Database=<db>;MultiSubnetFailover=True;Connect Timeout=30;ApplicationIntent=ReadWrite;Encrypt=True;TrustServerCertificate=True"}	null	low	t	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.20476
