1091	sqlserver	instruct	Increase health check failure threshold to tolerate restart window	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["unhealthy_threshold: Number of consecutive failures before marking down (recommend 5 for restart tolerance)", "probe_interval: 15-30 seconds recommended", "restart_timeout: Typical SQL Server restart is 2-5 minutes; size threshold accordingly"], "description": "For planned restarts, temporarily increase the health check failure tolerance to prevent premature failover:\\n\\n1. Azure ILB: Increase 'unhealthyThreshold' from default (2) to 5-6 probes before marking backend unhealthy. This gives SQL Server ~60-90 seconds to restart without triggering backend removal.\\n\\n2. HAProxy: Set 'fall 5' to require 5 consecutive failures before removing the server from the pool. Set 'rise 2' to require 2 successes before re-adding.\\n\\n3. Application connection pool: Set retry logic with exponential backoff (e.g., 3 retries with 5/10/20 second intervals) to handle transient connection failures during restart.\\n\\n4. For planned maintenance: Drain connections from the node first using AG manual failover to secondary, then restart SQL Server on the former primary while it is in secondary role — eliminating any health check impact on production traffic.\\n\\nAfter restart completes, restore original thresholds."}	null	medium	t	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.204764
