1110	sqlserver	verify	Confirm quorum vote distribution is correct and stable	{"sql": "SELECT c.quorum_type_desc, c.quorum_state_desc,\\n  cm.member_name, cm.member_type_desc, cm.member_state_desc,\\n  cm.number_of_quorum_votes\\nFROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster c\\nCROSS JOIN sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members cm\\nORDER BY cm.number_of_quorum_votes DESC, cm.member_name;", "parameters": [], "description": "Verify the vote distribution now reflects the intended configuration: all healthy production nodes hold their expected votes, total votes provide a safe majority under single-failure scenarios, and quorum_state_desc is NORMAL_QUORUM."}	null	low	f	t	00:01:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.226574
1119	sqlserver	instruct	Re-synchronize Windows Time service on drifted nodes	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["ntp_server_address"], "description": "On each node showing clock drift, open an elevated PowerShell or Command Prompt and run the following sequence: (1) Stop and restart the time service: net stop w32tm && net start w32tm. (2) Re-register the time service: w32tm /unregister && w32tm /register. (3) Force re-sync with domain hierarchy: w32tm /resync /force. (4) If the node is the PDC Emulator or a standalone server, configure an external NTP source: w32tm /config /manualpeerlist:'0.pool.ntp.org,1.pool.ntp.org' /syncfromflags:manual /reliable:YES /update && net stop w32tm && net start w32tm. (5) Verify sync: w32tm /query /status. (6) Confirm stratum is 2 or 3 and the source matches the expected NTP server."}	null	low	f	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.226576
1112	sqlserver	instruct	Re-add evicted node to cluster if appropriate	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["EvictedNodeName: Windows cluster node name of the evicted node", "AGName: Availability Group name", "DBName: Each AG database requiring HADR RESUME"], "description": "If the evicted node should be returned to the cluster:\\n\\n1. Confirm the node's OS and SQL Server are healthy:\\n   - Windows Server service: running\\n   - SQL Server service: running\\n   - Network connectivity: ping cluster nodes from evicted node and vice versa\\n\\n2. Re-add the evicted node to the cluster from Failover Cluster Manager:\\n   - Connect to an existing cluster node\\n   - Right-click cluster name > Add Node\\n   - Follow wizard to add the previously evicted node\\n\\n3. PowerShell alternative:\\n   Add-ClusterNode -Name <EvictedNodeName>\\n\\n4. After node rejoins, verify it reconnects to the AG:\\n   ALTER AVAILABILITY GROUP [<AGName>] JOIN;\\n   -- If databases are not automatically resumed:\\n   ALTER DATABASE [<DBName>] SET HADR RESUME;\\n\\n5. If node was the AG primary before eviction: do NOT fail back automatically. Allow synchronization to complete, then perform a planned failover if desired during next maintenance window.\\n\\nIf the node should remain out of the cluster (permanent decommission): adjust quorum configuration to account for the reduced node count (add witness if now even, or adjust NodeWeight values)."}	null	medium	t	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.226576
1113	sqlserver	instruct	Implement quorum impact check procedure for future node evictions	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["NodeToEvict: The name of the node being considered for eviction"], "description": "Establish an operational procedure to prevent future unsafe evictions:\\n\\n1. Create a pre-eviction checklist runbook that requires:\\n   a. Calculate post-eviction vote count: does removing this node leave majority votes?\\n      -- Run this query before any eviction:\\n      SELECT SUM(number_of_quorum_votes) - MAX(CASE WHEN member_name = '<NodeToEvict>' THEN number_of_quorum_votes ELSE 0 END) AS votes_after_eviction,\\n             SUM(number_of_quorum_votes) / 2 AS minimum_required\\n      FROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members WHERE member_state_desc = 'UP';\\n   b. Confirm votes_after_eviction > minimum_required before proceeding.\\n   c. If not: add a witness or adjust node weights before evicting.\\n\\n2. For planned maintenance (patching, hardware replacement): Use AG failover before node eviction to move AG roles away from the target node first.\\n\\n3. Require DBA sign-off on any node eviction that touches a node hosting an AG replica.\\n\\n4. Document the pre-eviction check in change management procedures and require it as a mandatory pre-condition for cluster node changes."}	null	low	f	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.226577
1114	sqlserver	verify	Assess surviving cluster state and quorum viability	{"sql": "SELECT\\n  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members WHERE member_state_desc = 'UP' AND member_type_desc = 'CLUSTER_NODE') AS surviving_nodes,\\n  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members WHERE member_type_desc = 'CLUSTER_NODE') AS total_nodes,\\n  (SELECT SUM(number_of_quorum_votes) FROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members WHERE member_state_desc = 'UP') AS active_votes,\\n  (SELECT SUM(number_of_quorum_votes) FROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members) AS total_votes,\\n  c.quorum_state_desc,\\n  ags.synchronization_health_desc\\nFROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster c\\nCROSS JOIN sys.dm_hadr_availability_group_states ags;", "parameters": [], "description": "Determine how many nodes survive, current vote totals, and whether quorum is still held. If active_votes > total_votes / 2, quorum is maintained and failover is not yet required."}	null	low	f	t	00:01:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.226578
1115	sqlserver	instruct	Isolate and halt failing nodes to stop cascade	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["failing_node_name"], "description": "On each node confirmed as failing or flapping: (1) In Failover Cluster Manager, right-click the node and select 'Stop Cluster Service'. (2) If the node is unresponsive, use the WSFC PowerShell cmdlet on a surviving node: Stop-ClusterNode -Name '<failing_node_name>'. (3) Do NOT allow failing nodes to rejoin until the root infrastructure cause (memory pressure, I/O storm, network partition) is resolved. This prevents the cascade from consuming additional healthy nodes."}	null	medium	t	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.226578
1117	sqlserver	verify	Confirm AG health and re-synchronize replicas	{"sql": "SELECT\\n  ag.name AS ag_name,\\n  ar.replica_server_name,\\n  ars.role_desc,\\n  ars.operational_state_desc,\\n  ars.synchronization_health_desc,\\n  ars.connected_state_desc,\\n  drs.synchronization_state_desc,\\n  drs.log_send_queue_size,\\n  drs.redo_queue_size\\nFROM sys.availability_groups ag\\nJOIN sys.availability_replicas ar ON ag.group_id = ar.group_id\\nJOIN sys.dm_hadr_availability_replica_states ars ON ar.replica_id = ars.replica_id\\nLEFT JOIN sys.dm_hadr_database_replica_states drs ON ar.replica_id = drs.replica_id\\nORDER BY ag.name, ars.role_desc;", "parameters": [], "description": "Confirm the AG has a healthy primary, replicas are reconnecting, and log send/redo queues are draining. Allow several minutes for log hardening on reconnected replicas before declaring the cascade fully resolved."}	null	low	f	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.22658
1118	sqlserver	verify	Measure clock skew on all cluster nodes	{"sql": "-- Run on each cluster node to record local time\\nSELECT\\n  SERVERPROPERTY('MachineName') AS node_name,\\n  GETDATE() AS local_time,\\n  GETUTCDATE() AS utc_time,\\n  SYSDATETIMEOFFSET() AS time_with_offset;", "parameters": [], "description": "Record the local time on each cluster node. Compare GETUTCDATE() values across nodes. A difference greater than 5 minutes will cause Kerberos authentication failures. A difference greater than 30 seconds can cause heartbeat instability. Also run 'w32tm /query /status' on each node in PowerShell to see NTP sync status and stratum."}	null	low	f	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.22658
1120	sqlserver	configure	Enforce NTP Group Policy and set VM clock synchronization	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["ntp_server_address", "hypervisor_type"], "description": "To prevent recurrence: (1) Via Group Policy (gpmc.msc), navigate to Computer Configuration > Administrative Templates > System > Windows Time Service > Time Providers. Enable 'Configure Windows NTP Client' and set NTPServer to your AD PDC Emulator or reliable NTP source. (2) For cluster nodes running as VMs, disable hypervisor time synchronization to prevent the hypervisor clock from overriding domain NTP: In Hyper-V Manager, uncheck 'Time synchronization' in VM Integration Services. For VMware: add 'tools.syncTime = FALSE' and 'time.synchronize.continue = FALSE' to the VM's .vmx file. (3) Ensure all nodes sync to the same NTP stratum hierarchy."}	{"sql": null, "description": "To revert VM time sync change: Re-enable Hyper-V Time Synchronization in VM Integration Services, or remove the VMware .vmx entries and restart VMware Tools. Re-run w32tm /resync /force after re-enabling."}	low	f	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.226582
1121	sqlserver	verify	Confirm cluster heartbeat stability and Kerberos auth	{"sql": "SELECT\\n  cm.member_name,\\n  cm.member_state_desc,\\n  c.quorum_state_desc,\\n  ags.synchronization_health_desc\\nFROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster c\\nCROSS JOIN sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members cm\\nCROSS JOIN sys.dm_hadr_availability_group_states ags\\nWHERE cm.member_type_desc = 'CLUSTER_NODE'\\nORDER BY cm.member_name;", "parameters": [], "description": "All cluster nodes should show member_state_desc = 'UP'. Run 'klist tickets' on each node to confirm Kerberos ticket issuance is working. Also run 'w32tm /monitor' to verify all nodes are within acceptable drift of each other (< 1 second for stability). If any node shows Kerberos errors, run 'klist purge' and re-authenticate."}	null	low	f	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.226582
1122	sqlserver	verify	Identify both partitions and determine data currency	{"sql": "-- Run on each partition's primary to compare LSNs\\nSELECT\\n  SERVERPROPERTY('ServerName') AS server_name,\\n  drs.database_id,\\n  DB_NAME(drs.database_id) AS db_name,\\n  drs.last_commit_lsn,\\n  drs.last_commit_time,\\n  drs.log_send_queue_size,\\n  ars.role_desc,\\n  ars.synchronization_health_desc\\nFROM sys.dm_hadr_database_replica_states drs\\nJOIN sys.dm_hadr_availability_replica_states ars ON drs.replica_id = ars.replica_id\\nWHERE ars.is_local = 1\\nORDER BY drs.database_id;", "parameters": [], "description": "Run this query on the primary replica in EACH partition. Compare last_commit_lsn and last_commit_time to determine which partition has the most recent committed transactions. The partition with the higher last_commit_lsn is the authoritative one. Document the LSN gap to assess data loss magnitude."}	null	low	f	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.226583
1124	sqlserver	instruct	Restore full quorum on authoritative partition and verify primary	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["ag_name"], "description": "On the authoritative partition: (1) Confirm WSFC quorum is held: Get-ClusterQuorum in PowerShell. If quorum is lost due to the partition re-balancing, run: Start-ClusterNode -FixQuorum on the primary node. (2) Confirm SQL Server AG has a single primary: SELECT role_desc, replica_server_name FROM sys.dm_hadr_availability_replica_states ars JOIN sys.availability_replicas ar ON ars.replica_id = ar.replica_id. There must be exactly one PRIMARY. (3) Verify applications are reconnecting to the listener: SELECT * FROM sys.availability_group_listeners. (4) Adjust quorum votes if needed using PowerShell: (Get-ClusterNode '<node_name>').NodeWeight = 1."}	null	medium	t	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.226584
1125	sqlserver	instruct	Reconcile diverged data and re-seed non-authoritative replicas	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["ag_name", "non_auth_server", "db_name", "backup_path"], "description": "To restore the non-authoritative nodes as healthy replicas: (1) For any databases where the non-authoritative partition processed uncommitted transactions during split-brain, assess divergence via backup/log analysis and work with application teams to replay missing transactions if business requirements demand. (2) Remove the diverged replicas from the AG: ALTER AVAILABILITY GROUP [<ag_name>] REMOVE REPLICA ON '<non_auth_server>'. (3) Take a full backup from the authoritative primary: BACKUP DATABASE [<db_name>] TO DISK = '<backup_path>' WITH COMPRESSION, COPY_ONLY. (4) Restore with NORECOVERY on the non-authoritative node: RESTORE DATABASE [<db_name>] FROM DISK = '<backup_path>' WITH NORECOVERY. (5) Re-add the replica: ALTER AVAILABILITY GROUP [<ag_name>] ADD REPLICA ON '<non_auth_server>' WITH (ENDPOINT_URL = 'TCP://<server>:5022', AVAILABILITY_MODE = SYNCHRONOUS_COMMIT, FAILOVER_MODE = AUTOMATIC). (6) Join the database: ALTER DATABASE [<db_name>] SET HADR AVAILABILITY GROUP = [<ag_name>]."}	{"sql": null, "description": "If re-seeding fails, use automatic seeding: ALTER AVAILABILITY GROUP [<ag_name>] MODIFY REPLICA ON '<non_auth_server>' WITH (SEEDING_MODE = AUTOMATIC). Monitor with: SELECT start_time, completion_time, performed_seeding FROM sys.dm_hadr_automatic_seeding."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.229872
1126	sqlserver	verify	Document current cluster topology and failure tolerance gap	{"sql": "SELECT\\n  cm.member_name,\\n  cm.member_type_desc,\\n  cm.member_state_desc,\\n  cm.number_of_quorum_votes,\\n  c.quorum_type_desc,\\n  CASE\\n    WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members WHERE member_type_desc = 'CLUSTER_NODE') = 2\\n      AND (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members WHERE member_type_desc <> 'CLUSTER_NODE') = 0\\n    THEN 'CRITICAL: 2-node no-witness can tolerate 0 node failures'\\n    WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members WHERE member_type_desc = 'CLUSTER_NODE') = 2\\n    THEN 'MINIMAL: 2-node with witness tolerates 1 failure but witness is single point'\\n    ELSE 'Calculate: floor(total_votes / 2) failures tolerated'\\n  END AS tolerance_assessment\\nFROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster c\\nCROSS JOIN sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members cm\\nORDER BY cm.member_type_desc, cm.member_name;", "parameters": [], "description": "Document the existing node count, quorum model, vote distribution, and tolerance gap. A 2-node cluster with no witness has zero failure tolerance. A 3-node cluster tolerates 1 failure. Determine target node count based on required simultaneous failure tolerance."}	null	low	f	t	00:01:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.230419
7966	postgresql	verify	Verify remaining cluster has sufficient nodes	{"sql": "SELECT (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM pg_stat_replication) + 1 AS total_nodes,\\n  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM pg_stat_replication) AS standby_count;", "parameters": [], "description": "Confirms the remaining cluster has enough nodes for HA operation"}	\N	low	f	t	seconds	2026-02-25 08:59:43.77256
1127	sqlserver	instruct	Add new nodes to WSFC cluster	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["new_node_name"], "description": "For each new server being added to the cluster: (1) On the new server, open Server Manager > Add Roles and Features > add 'Failover Clustering' feature. (2) Run Cluster Validation from Failover Cluster Manager: Validate a Configuration > add all existing nodes plus the new node. Review and address any warnings. (3) Add the node from Failover Cluster Manager: right-click the cluster name > Add Node. Follow the wizard selecting the new server. (4) Via PowerShell on an existing node: Add-ClusterNode -Name '<new_node_name>'. (5) Set the quorum vote weight for the new node: (Get-ClusterNode '<new_node_name>').NodeWeight = 1. (6) Verify the node is UP: Get-ClusterNode."}	{"sql": null, "description": "To remove a newly added node: Remove-ClusterNode -Name '<new_node_name>' -Force in PowerShell. This does not affect existing cluster members."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.230985
1130	sqlserver	verify	Confirm shared infrastructure is restored and assess scope	{"sql": "-- Run on any accessible node after infrastructure is back\\nSELECT\\n  cm.member_name,\\n  cm.member_state_desc,\\n  cm.number_of_quorum_votes,\\n  c.quorum_state_desc,\\n  (SELECT SUM(io_stall_read_ms + io_stall_write_ms) / NULLIF(SUM(num_of_reads + num_of_writes), 0)\\n   FROM sys.dm_io_virtual_file_stats(NULL, NULL)) AS avg_io_stall_ms,\\n  (SELECT outstanding_disk_io_count FROM sys.dm_os_schedulers WHERE status = 'VISIBLE ONLINE' AND scheduler_id < 255 ORDER BY scheduler_id OFFSET 0 ROWS FETCH NEXT 1 ROWS ONLY) AS pending_io_count\\nFROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster c\\nCROSS JOIN sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members cm\\nORDER BY cm.member_state_desc;", "parameters": [], "description": "Identify which nodes are UP vs DOWN and check I/O health. High avg_io_stall_ms (>200ms) indicates storage is still recovering. Verify with the storage team that all LUNs/volumes used by SQL Server are online and consistent before proceeding to bring SQL Server online."}	null	low	f	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.232952
1132	sqlserver	verify	Confirm AG health and database consistency after recovery	{"sql": "-- Verify AG state and database consistency\\nSELECT\\n  ag.name AS ag_name,\\n  ar.replica_server_name,\\n  ars.role_desc,\\n  ars.operational_state_desc,\\n  ars.synchronization_health_desc,\\n  ars.connected_state_desc,\\n  drs.database_id,\\n  DB_NAME(drs.database_id) AS db_name,\\n  drs.synchronization_state_desc,\\n  drs.is_suspended,\\n  drs.suspend_reason_desc,\\n  drs.log_send_queue_size,\\n  drs.redo_queue_size\\nFROM sys.availability_groups ag\\nJOIN sys.availability_replicas ar ON ag.group_id = ar.group_id\\nJOIN sys.dm_hadr_availability_replica_states ars ON ar.replica_id = ars.replica_id\\nLEFT JOIN sys.dm_hadr_database_replica_states drs ON ar.replica_id = drs.replica_id\\nORDER BY ag.name, ars.role_desc, DB_NAME(drs.database_id);\\n\\n-- Check for databases in suspect state\\nSELECT name, state_desc, user_access_desc\\nFROM sys.databases\\nWHERE state_desc NOT IN ('ONLINE') AND name NOT IN ('tempdb');", "parameters": [], "description": "Verify that all databases are ONLINE (not SUSPECT or RECOVERY_PENDING), the AG has exactly one PRIMARY, and replicas are re-synchronizing (redo_queue_size decreasing). If any database is in SUSPECT state, it requires individual database recovery procedures."}	null	low	f	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.232958
1386	sqlserver	verify	Confirm parallel redo threads are active and redo lag is decreasing	{"sql": "SELECT command, COUNT(*) AS thread_count FROM sys.dm_exec_requests WHERE command LIKE 'PARALLEL REDO%' OR command = 'DB STARTUP' GROUP BY command; SELECT drs.redo_queue_size, drs.redo_rate, drs.synchronization_state_desc FROM sys.dm_hadr_database_replica_states drs WHERE drs.is_local = 1 AND drs.is_primary_replica = 0;", "parameters": {}, "description": "Verify multiple 'PARALLEL REDO' worker threads appear and redo_rate has increased, with redo_queue_size trending toward zero."}	null	low	f	t	00:10:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.257348
1133	sqlserver	instruct	Address root infrastructure cause and implement redundancy improvements	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "After immediate recovery, address the shared infrastructure failure to prevent recurrence: (1) Power failures: Verify UPS capacity and battery health for all nodes; implement redundant power feeds from separate circuits where possible; configure generator auto-start testing schedule. (2) Network switch failures: Ensure cluster nodes have NIC teaming (LBFO or SET) across physically separate switches; verify dedicated cluster heartbeat network is on a separate switch from application traffic. (3) Storage array failures: Confirm storage multipath I/O (MPIO) is configured and active; verify RAID protection level is appropriate; test storage failover with the storage vendor. (4) Review cluster design for any remaining single points of failure and document findings for capacity planning."}	null	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.233909
1134	sqlserver	verify	Confirm witness unreachability and identify failure point	{"sql": "SELECT\\n  cm.member_name AS witness_name,\\n  cm.member_type_desc,\\n  cm.member_state_desc,\\n  cm.number_of_quorum_votes,\\n  c.quorum_type_desc,\\n  c.quorum_state_desc\\nFROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster c\\nCROSS JOIN sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members cm\\nWHERE cm.member_type_desc <> 'CLUSTER_NODE'\\nORDER BY cm.member_type_desc;", "parameters": ["witness_server"], "description": "Confirm the witness is showing member_state_desc = 'DOWN' or 'UNKNOWN'. Then from a cluster node, run network diagnostics in PowerShell: (1) Test-NetConnection -ComputerName '<witness_server>' -Port 445 (for file share witness). (2) Resolve-DnsName '<witness_server>' to check DNS resolution. (3) Test-Connection '<witness_server>' -Count 4 for basic ICMP reachability. Document where connectivity breaks."}	null	low	f	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236518
1171	sqlserver	verify	Confirm cloud witness is active and quorum is normal	{"sql": "SELECT cm.member_name, cm.member_type_desc, cm.member_state_desc,\\n  cm.number_of_quorum_votes,\\n  c.quorum_type_desc, c.quorum_state_desc\\nFROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster c\\nCROSS JOIN sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members cm\\nORDER BY cm.member_type_desc, cm.member_name;", "parameters": [], "description": "Confirm that the cloud witness member_state_desc = 'UP' and quorum_state_desc = 'NORMAL_QUORUM'. If the cluster shows CLOUD_WITNESS in quorum_type_desc, the witness type is correctly configured."}	null	low	f	t	00:01:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236546
9995	postgresql	verify	Confirm feedback visible on primary	{"sql": "-- Run on PRIMARY:\\nSELECT client_addr, application_name, backend_xmin FROM pg_stat_replication;", "description": "Verify backend_xmin is now populated for the replica"}	\N	low	f	t	10 seconds	2026-02-25 08:59:43.77256
1135	sqlserver	configure	Resolve network path or firewall blocking witness access	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["witness_server", "cluster_subnet_cidr", "adapter_name"], "description": "Based on the failure point identified: (1) Firewall blocking: On the witness server, open Windows Firewall with Advanced Security and verify inbound rules allow File and Printer Sharing (SMB-In) on TCP 445 from the cluster node subnet. Add rule if missing: New-NetFirewallRule -DisplayName 'WSFC Witness SMB' -Direction Inbound -Protocol TCP -LocalPort 445 -RemoteAddress '<cluster_subnet_cidr>' -Action Allow. (2) Routing issue: Run tracert '<witness_server>' from a cluster node to identify the broken hop. Engage network team to restore the route. (3) VLAN misconfiguration: Verify the cluster nodes' cluster network adapter and the witness server are on the same VLAN or have a routed path between them. (4) NIC failure on witness: Restart network adapter on witness server: Restart-NetAdapter -Name '<adapter_name>'."}	{"sql": null, "description": "To remove the firewall rule added: Remove-NetFirewallRule -DisplayName 'WSFC Witness SMB'."}	low	f	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236523
1136	sqlserver	verify	Confirm witness is UP and quorum is healthy	{"sql": "SELECT\\n  cm.member_name,\\n  cm.member_type_desc,\\n  cm.member_state_desc,\\n  cm.number_of_quorum_votes,\\n  c.quorum_state_desc\\nFROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster c\\nCROSS JOIN sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members cm\\nORDER BY cm.member_type_desc, cm.member_name;", "parameters": [], "description": "After restoring network connectivity, the WSFC cluster service should automatically detect the witness becoming reachable within 1-2 heartbeat intervals (typically 5-10 seconds). Verify member_state_desc = 'UP' for the witness and quorum_state_desc = 'QUORUM_PRESENT'. If the witness does not come back automatically within 60 seconds, restart the Cluster Service on one node: Restart-Service ClusSvc."}	null	low	f	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236523
1139	sqlserver	verify	Validate witness recovery and optionally migrate to cloud witness	{"sql": "SELECT\\n  cm.member_name,\\n  cm.member_type_desc,\\n  cm.member_state_desc,\\n  cm.number_of_quorum_votes,\\n  c.quorum_state_desc\\nFROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster c\\nCROSS JOIN sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members cm\\nORDER BY cm.member_type_desc;", "parameters": ["azure_storage_account", "key"], "description": "Confirm the witness is UP and quorum_state_desc = 'QUORUM_PRESENT'. If the file share server is itself a potential single point of failure (same location as cluster nodes, unreliable server), consider migrating to a cloud witness for higher availability: Set-ClusterQuorum -CloudWitness -AccountName '<azure_storage_account>' -AccessKey '<key>'. A cloud witness eliminates the dependency on local file server infrastructure."}	null	low	f	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236526
5095	sqlserver	verify	Confirm legacy clients are upgraded and encryption is enabled	{"sql": "SELECT c.encrypt_option, s.client_interface_name, s.client_version,\\n  COUNT(*) AS connections\\nFROM sys.dm_exec_connections c\\nJOIN sys.dm_exec_sessions s ON c.session_id = s.session_id\\nWHERE s.is_user_process = 1\\nGROUP BY c.encrypt_option, s.client_interface_name, s.client_version;", "parameters": [], "description": "Verify all clients are using modern drivers with encryption."}	null	low	f	t	00:01:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236527
1140	sqlserver	verify	Confirm cloud witness state and internet connectivity	{"sql": "SELECT\\n  cm.member_name,\\n  cm.member_type_desc,\\n  cm.member_state_desc,\\n  cm.number_of_quorum_votes,\\n  c.quorum_type_desc,\\n  c.quorum_state_desc\\nFROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster c\\nCROSS JOIN sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members cm\\nORDER BY cm.member_type_desc;", "parameters": ["storage_account"], "description": "Confirm the witness type is CLOUD and it shows member_state_desc = 'DOWN'. Then test internet connectivity from each cluster node in PowerShell: (1) Test basic internet: Test-NetConnection -ComputerName '8.8.8.8' -Port 443. (2) Test Azure Blob Storage endpoint: Test-NetConnection -ComputerName '<storage_account>.blob.core.windows.net' -Port 443. (3) If behind a proxy, check proxy settings: netsh winhttp show proxy. (4) Check DNS: Resolve-DnsName '<storage_account>.blob.core.windows.net'."}	null	low	f	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236527
1141	sqlserver	configure	Restore internet connectivity or configure proxy for cluster service	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["proxy_server", "proxy_port", "storage_account", "new_key"], "description": "If connectivity is blocked by a proxy or firewall: (1) Configure WinHTTP proxy for the cluster service (runs as SYSTEM): netsh winhttp set proxy '<proxy_server>:<port>' '<bypass_list>'. (2) Verify the proxy has access to Azure Blob: Test-NetConnection -ComputerName '<storage_account>.blob.core.windows.net' -Port 443. (3) If a firewall rule was added that blocks Azure storage, remove or update it: coordinate with the network team to add an exception for '<storage_account>.blob.core.windows.net' on TCP 443. (4) If the Azure storage account key has been rotated, update the witness: Set-ClusterQuorum -CloudWitness -AccountName '<storage_account>' -AccessKey '<new_key>'. Key rotation is a common cause of cloud witness failure."}	{"sql": null, "description": "To remove WinHTTP proxy: netsh winhttp reset proxy. To revert to old storage key: Set-ClusterQuorum -CloudWitness -AccountName '<storage_account>' -AccessKey '<old_key>'."}	low	f	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236528
