1197	sqlserver	instruct	Free disk space on the current volume	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "Free disk space on the current volume using OS-level operations before attempting to relocate files. Options: (1) Delete old backup files from the volume if backup files are co-located. (2) Move non-database files to another volume. (3) Use Windows Disk Cleanup or server-side tools to clear temp files. (4) Coordinate with storage team to expand the volume (LUN extension). After freeing space, verify autogrowth can now succeed by checking volume_free_gb exceeds the autogrowth increment."}	null	medium	t	f	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236565
1145	sqlserver	instruct	Validate and repair cluster computer account in Active Directory	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["ClusterName"], "description": "In Active Directory Users and Computers (or PowerShell with ActiveDirectory module): (1) Locate the cluster computer account: Get-ADComputer -Identity '<ClusterName>' -Properties Enabled, LockedOut, PasswordExpired, PasswordLastSet. (2) If the account is disabled: Enable-ADAccount -Identity '<ClusterName>$'. (3) If the account password is expired or corrupted: Reset-ComputerMachinePassword for the cluster is done via the cluster service, not AD directly. Instead, disable and re-enable the account to force a password reset: Disable-ADAccount '<ClusterName>$'; Enable-ADAccount '<ClusterName>$'. (4) On a cluster node, run: Test-ComputerSecureChannel -Repair -Credential (Get-Credential). (5) Verify Kerberos ticket acquisition: klist tickets — look for the cluster service account. (6) Purge stale tickets: klist purge."}	null	medium	t	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236531
