1148	sqlserver	verify	Assess disk witness state and storage path availability	{"sql": "SELECT\\n  cm.member_name AS witness_resource,\\n  cm.member_type_desc,\\n  cm.member_state_desc,\\n  cm.number_of_quorum_votes,\\n  c.quorum_type_desc,\\n  c.quorum_state_desc\\nFROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster c\\nCROSS JOIN sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members cm\\nWHERE c.quorum_type_desc LIKE '%DISK%'\\n   OR cm.member_type_desc LIKE '%DISK%'\\nORDER BY cm.member_type_desc;", "parameters": [], "description": "Confirm the disk witness is DOWN. Then check disk availability from Windows Disk Management: (1) On the node currently owning the quorum disk resource: Get-ClusterResource | Where-Object ResourceType -eq 'Physical Disk' | Format-List Name, State, OwnerNode. (2) Check if the disk is visible to Windows: Get-Disk | Where-Object IsOffline -eq $true. (3) Check for I/O errors in Event Log: Get-WinEvent -LogName System | Where-Object {$_.Id -in @(7, 11, 51, 153)} | Select-Object -First 20. Document whether the disk is missing (SAN path issue) or visible but offline/corrupted."}	null	low	f	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236533
