1170	sqlserver	instruct	Reconfigure or regenerate cloud witness credentials	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "If the storage account access key has been rotated since the witness was configured, the cluster will silently fail to authenticate: (1) In the Azure Portal, navigate to the Storage Account → Security + Networking → Access Keys. (2) Regenerate key2 (keep key1 active during rotation). (3) Update the cloud witness: 'Set-ClusterQuorum -CloudWitness -AccountName \\"<storage_account>\\" -AccessKey \\"<new_key>\\"'. (4) If the storage account's firewall restricts access, add the rootcause IP addresses of all cluster nodes to the allowed list under Networking → Firewalls and virtual networks."}	null	low	t	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236545
1172	sqlserver	verify	Identify the stale configuration element	{"sql": "SELECT cm.member_name, cm.member_type_desc, cm.member_state_desc,\\n  cm.number_of_quorum_votes,\\n  c.quorum_type_desc, c.quorum_state_desc,\\n  (SELECT SUM(number_of_quorum_votes) FROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members WHERE member_state_desc = 'UP') AS active_votes\\nFROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster c\\nCROSS JOIN sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members cm\\nORDER BY cm.member_type_desc;", "parameters": [], "description": "Check the cluster's current quorum type and witness state. Cross-reference with the infrastructure change log to identify whether the stale element is: (1) a file share path (server renamed or share moved), (2) a cloud witness storage account key (key rotated), or (3) a witness server IP (IP address changed). Run 'Get-ClusterQuorum' in PowerShell to see the current witness path."}	null	low	f	t	00:01:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236547
