2293	sqlserver	instruct	Implement patch coordination policy and access controls to prevent recurrence	{"sql": "-- Audit current sysadmin role members who have access to patch AG nodes\\nSELECT sp.name AS login_name, sp.type_desc,\\n  spr.name AS role_name\\nFROM sys.server_principals sp\\nJOIN sys.server_role_members srm ON sp.principal_id = srm.member_principal_id\\nJOIN sys.server_principals spr ON srm.role_principal_id = spr.principal_id\\nWHERE spr.name IN ('sysadmin', 'serveradmin')\\n  AND sp.type IN ('S', 'U', 'G')\\nORDER BY sp.name;", "parameters": {}, "description": "Establish a formal patch coordination policy: (1) All AG patch windows require a single named patch coordinator and a change management ticket listing all participating administrators. (2) No administrator applies patches to AG nodes outside of an approved, coordinated window. (3) Use SQL Server patch automation tools (SQL Server Update Services, or WSUS/SCCM) to centralize patch delivery rather than allowing individual administrators to download and apply patches independently. (4) After each patch window, verify all replicas show identical ProductVersion via linked server queries or a monitoring dashboard. (5) Consider implementing Patch My PC, ManageEngine Patch Manager, or WSUS with SQL Server detection rules to enforce uniform patching across all AG nodes. Review sysadmin membership and restrict OS-level patch application rights to the designated coordinator account."}	null	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.386632
2295	sqlserver	execute	Re-apply the patch on the target node with coordinated suspension	{"sql": "-- Before patching: suspend data movement on the secondary being patched\\n-- Run on PRIMARY:\\nSELECT name FROM sys.databases WHERE database_id > 4 AND is_read_only = 0;\\n-- Then on the SECONDARY node being patched:\\n-- ALTER DATABASE [YourDB1] SET HADR SUSPEND;\\n-- ALTER DATABASE [YourDB2] SET HADR SUSPEND;\\n-- (repeat for all AG databases)\\n\\n-- Apply patch (OS process on target node):\\n-- <CU_Installer.exe> /QUIET /ACTION=Patch /INSTANCENAME=MSSQLSERVER /IACCEPTSQLSERVERLICENSETERMS\\n-- SQL Server service restarts automatically\\n\\n-- After restart on TARGET node, verify version and resume data movement:\\nSELECT SERVERPROPERTY('ProductVersion') AS version,\\n  SERVERPROPERTY('ProductUpdateLevel') AS cu_level;\\n\\n-- Resume HADR on TARGET node after confirming correct version:\\n-- ALTER DATABASE [YourDB1] SET HADR RESUME;\\n-- ALTER DATABASE [YourDB2] SET HADR RESUME;", "parameters": {"quiet_install": true, "installer_action": "Patch"}, "description": "Applies the patch on the previously-failed node following the same rolling upgrade procedure used for other nodes. Suspend data movement before starting the installer. After the installer completes and SQL Server restarts, verify the version matches the other patched nodes, then resume data movement and wait for SYNCHRONIZED state."}	{"sql": "-- If patch fails again: uninstall via Control Panel > Programs > SQL Server CU\\n-- After uninstall and restart:\\n-- ALTER DATABASE [YourDB] SET HADR RESUME;\\n-- Verify replica re-joins AG and examine Setup log for new failure reason", "description": "Uninstall the CU, restart SQL Server, and resume data movement. The node will operate at the lower version temporarily while root cause is fully resolved."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.386633
2691	sqlserver	execute	Enable optimize for ad hoc workloads	{"sql": "-- Enable optimize for ad hoc workloads (stores plan stub on first execution,\\n-- full plan only on second execution — reduces cache bloat with no downtime)\\nEXEC sp_configure 'show advanced options', 1;\\nRECONFIGURE;\\nEXEC sp_configure 'optimize for ad hoc workloads', 1;\\nRECONFIGURE;\\n\\n-- Verify\\nSELECT name, value_in_use\\nFROM sys.configurations\\nWHERE name = 'optimize for ad hoc workloads'", "parameters": {"optimize for ad hoc workloads": 1}, "description": "This is a safe, online change requiring no restart. New ad-hoc queries will store a plan stub (not a full plan) until executed a second time, dramatically reducing single-use plan cache bloat."}	{"sql": "EXEC sp_configure 'optimize for ad hoc workloads', 0;\\nRECONFIGURE;", "description": "Revert if unintended plan caching behaviour is observed."}	low	f	t	00:02:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.387302
2296	sqlserver	verify	Run DBCC CHECKDB as post-patch validation and confirm AG synchronization	{"sql": "-- Verify patch applied correctly\\nSELECT SERVERPROPERTY('ServerName') AS node,\\n  SERVERPROPERTY('ProductVersion') AS version,\\n  SERVERPROPERTY('ProductUpdateLevel') AS cu_level;\\n\\n-- Verify AG replica is synchronized\\nSELECT ar.replica_server_name,\\n  ars.connected_state_desc,\\n  ars.synchronization_health_desc,\\n  drs.synchronization_state_desc,\\n  drs.log_send_queue_size,\\n  drs.redo_queue_size\\nFROM sys.availability_replicas ar\\nJOIN sys.dm_hadr_availability_replica_states ars ON ar.replica_id = ars.replica_id\\nLEFT JOIN sys.dm_hadr_database_replica_states drs ON ar.replica_id = drs.replica_id\\nWHERE ar.replica_server_name = @@SERVERNAME;\\n\\n-- Run DBCC CHECKDB on all user databases (post-patch integrity validation)\\n-- Schedule as a SQL Agent job if immediate run would impact users:\\n-- DBCC CHECKDB ([YourDB]) WITH NO_INFOMSGS, ALL_ERRORMSGS;\\n\\n-- Check last known good CHECKDB after validation completes:\\nSELECT name,\\n  DATABASEPROPERTYEX(name, 'LastGoodCheckDbTime') AS last_good_checkdb\\nFROM sys.databases\\nWHERE database_id > 4;", "parameters": {}, "description": "Validates that the patched node now shows the same ProductVersion and CU level as the other AG replicas, the replica is in CONNECTED and HEALTHY state, all databases are SYNCHRONIZED with zero queue sizes, and DBCC CHECKDB completes without errors on all user databases. DBCC CHECKDB is the key post-patch validation check that was previously blocked by the failed patch installation."}	null	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.387621
2299	sqlserver	verify	Confirm AG health, quorum state, and failover readiness with updated topology	{"sql": "-- Verify AG is healthy with updated replica count\\nSELECT ag.name AS ag_name,\\n  ags.synchronization_health_desc,\\n  ags.primary_replica,\\n  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM sys.availability_replicas ar2\\n   WHERE ar2.group_id = ag.group_id) AS total_replicas,\\n  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM sys.dm_hadr_availability_replica_states ars2\\n   JOIN sys.availability_replicas ar3 ON ars2.replica_id = ar3.replica_id\\n   WHERE ar3.group_id = ag.group_id\\n     AND ars2.connected_state_desc = 'CONNECTED') AS connected_replicas,\\n  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM sys.availability_replicas ar4\\n   WHERE ar4.group_id = ag.group_id\\n     AND ar4.failover_mode_desc = 'AUTOMATIC') AS auto_failover_replicas\\nFROM sys.availability_groups ag\\nJOIN sys.dm_hadr_availability_group_states ags ON ag.group_id = ags.group_id;\\n\\n-- Verify no disconnected replicas remain\\nSELECT ar.replica_server_name, ars.connected_state_desc,\\n  ars.synchronization_health_desc, drs.synchronization_state_desc\\nFROM sys.availability_replicas ar\\nJOIN sys.dm_hadr_availability_replica_states ars ON ar.replica_id = ars.replica_id\\nLEFT JOIN sys.dm_hadr_database_replica_states drs ON ar.replica_id = drs.replica_id;\\n\\n-- Verify cluster quorum via PowerShell:\\n-- EXEC xp_cmdshell 'powershell -Command \\"Get-ClusterQuorum; Get-ClusterNode | Select Name,State,NodeWeight\\"';", "parameters": {}, "description": "Confirms zero DISCONNECTED replicas in the AG, AG synchronization_health_desc is HEALTHY, connected_replicas equals total_replicas, and at least one auto_failover replica exists if automatic failover is required. Validates cluster quorum shows all remaining nodes in Up state with a witness configured if an even number of nodes remain."}	null	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.387626
2301	sqlserver	execute	Wait for data synchronization catch-up and verify replica health	{"sql": "-- Monitor log send and redo queue drain on the reconnected replica\\n-- Run this repeatedly until queues reach zero\\nSELECT ar.replica_server_name,\\n  drs.database_id,\\n  d.name AS database_name,\\n  drs.synchronization_state_desc,\\n  drs.log_send_queue_size / 1024.0 AS log_send_queue_mb,\\n  drs.log_send_rate / 1024.0 AS log_send_rate_mb_sec,\\n  drs.redo_queue_size / 1024.0 AS redo_queue_mb,\\n  drs.redo_rate / 1024.0 AS redo_rate_mb_sec,\\n  CASE WHEN drs.redo_rate > 0\\n    THEN drs.redo_queue_size / drs.redo_rate\\n    ELSE NULL\\n  END AS estimated_catchup_seconds\\nFROM sys.dm_hadr_database_replica_states drs\\nJOIN sys.availability_replicas ar ON drs.replica_id = ar.replica_id\\nJOIN sys.databases d ON drs.database_id = d.database_id\\nWHERE ar.replica_server_name = '<recovered_node_name>'\\nORDER BY drs.redo_queue_size DESC;\\n\\n-- Final health check after queues drain\\nSELECT ar.replica_server_name,\\n  ars.connected_state_desc,\\n  ars.synchronization_health_desc,\\n  drs.synchronization_state_desc\\nFROM sys.availability_replicas ar\\nJOIN sys.dm_hadr_availability_replica_states ars ON ar.replica_id = ars.replica_id\\nLEFT JOIN sys.dm_hadr_database_replica_states drs ON ar.replica_id = drs.replica_id\\nWHERE ar.replica_server_name = '<recovered_node_name>';", "parameters": {"sync_target_state": "SYNCHRONIZED", "target_queue_size_kb": 0, "polling_interval_seconds": 30}, "description": "After network restoration, the isolated replica must catch up on all transactions that occurred during the partition period. Monitor log_send_queue_size and redo_queue_size every 30 seconds. The estimated_catchup_seconds calculation provides an ETA. Do not proceed with patching until synchronization_state_desc = SYNCHRONIZED and both queue sizes are 0. Large log queues indicate significant catch-up work — wait for completion before introducing additional instability via patching."}	null	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.387628
2303	sqlserver	verify	Confirm version gap and clear transient blockers	{"sql": "-- Confirm current build and compare to expected CU build number\\nSELECT SERVERPROPERTY('ProductVersion')   AS current_version,\\n       SERVERPROPERTY('ProductUpdateLevel') AS current_cu,\\n       SERVERPROPERTY('ProductLevel')       AS product_level;\\n\\n-- Check for locked SQL Server files (setup will fail if binaries are held open)\\n-- Also verify temp space on system drive\\nSELECT vs.volume_mount_point,\\n       vs.available_bytes / 1073741824 AS available_gb\\nFROM   sys.master_files mf\\nCROSS  APPLY sys.dm_os_volume_stats(mf.database_id, mf.file_id) vs\\nWHERE  mf.database_id IN (1, 2, 3)\\nGROUP  BY vs.volume_mount_point, vs.available_bytes;", "parameters": {}, "description": "Record the current product version and CU level. Confirm available disk space on volumes that SQL Server setup will write to. Resolve any antivirus or backup agent file locks before proceeding."}	null	low	f	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.388626
3372	sqlserver	execute	Force immediate full-scan statistics update on high-modification indexes	{"sql": "-- Update statistics for each table with high modification_ratio\\n-- identified in the detection output\\nUPDATE STATISTICS <schema>.<table> [<index_name>]\\n    WITH FULLSCAN, NORECOMPUTE;\\n\\n-- For all indexes on a specific table:\\nUPDATE STATISTICS <schema>.<table> WITH FULLSCAN;", "parameters": {"table": "Table name with outdated statistics", "schema": "Schema of the target table", "index_name": "Optional: specific index statistics to update"}, "description": "Immediately refresh the histogram for each stale index using a full table scan to get the most accurate distribution data"}	null	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.389045
2311	sqlserver	verify	Apply missing CU to lagging replicas and confirm AG consistency	{"sql": "-- After applying patches, confirm all replicas are at the same level\\nSELECT ar.replica_server_name,\\n       ars.role_desc,\\n       ars.connected_state_desc,\\n       ars.synchronization_health_desc,\\n       SERVERPROPERTY('ProductVersion')   AS local_version,\\n       SERVERPROPERTY('ProductUpdateLevel') AS local_cu\\nFROM   sys.dm_hadr_availability_replica_states ars\\nJOIN   sys.availability_replicas ar ON ars.replica_id = ar.replica_id;\\n\\n-- Confirm all databases are SYNCHRONIZED\\nSELECT DB_NAME(drs.database_id) AS db_name,\\n       ar.replica_server_name,\\n       drs.synchronization_state_desc,\\n       drs.synchronization_health_desc\\nFROM   sys.dm_hadr_database_replica_states drs\\nJOIN   sys.availability_replicas ar ON drs.replica_id = ar.replica_id;", "parameters": {}, "description": "Using the controlled patching process (same installer, same flags as RC06 resolution), apply the target CU to any replica still below the expected build. Patch secondaries first, then fail over and patch the former primary. After all patches are applied, run the SQL above to confirm version uniformity and AG health."}	null	medium	f	t	01:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.389671
2312	sqlserver	verify	Confirm version gap and AG synchronization state on the returned node	{"sql": "-- Check version on the returned node\\nSELECT SERVERPROPERTY('ServerName')        AS server_name,\\n       SERVERPROPERTY('ProductVersion')     AS product_version,\\n       SERVERPROPERTY('ProductUpdateLevel') AS cu_level;\\n\\n-- Check current AG synchronization state — look for NOT SYNCHRONIZING or suspended databases\\nSELECT ag.name AS ag_name,\\n       ar.replica_server_name,\\n       ars.role_desc,\\n       ars.connected_state_desc,\\n       drs.synchronization_state_desc,\\n       drs.synchronization_health_desc,\\n       drs.is_suspended,\\n       drs.suspend_reason_desc,\\n       drs.log_send_queue_size,\\n       drs.redo_queue_size\\nFROM   sys.dm_hadr_database_replica_states drs\\nJOIN   sys.availability_replicas ar ON drs.replica_id = ar.replica_id\\nJOIN   sys.availability_groups ag ON ar.group_id = ag.group_id;", "parameters": {}, "description": "Confirm this node's build is behind the primary and identify which AG databases are not synchronizing or suspended. Record log_send_queue_size and redo_queue_size to estimate catch-up time after patching."}	null	low	f	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.389672
2314	sqlserver	verify	Resume data movement and confirm full synchronization	{"sql": "-- Resume any suspended databases on this replica\\n-- Run on the PRIMARY for each database that is suspended on the returned secondary\\nALTER DATABASE [<database_name>] SET HADR RESUME;\\n\\n-- Monitor redo queue drain — run repeatedly until redo_queue_size reaches 0\\nSELECT ar.replica_server_name,\\n       DB_NAME(drs.database_id)        AS database_name,\\n       drs.synchronization_state_desc,\\n       drs.synchronization_health_desc,\\n       drs.redo_queue_size             AS redo_queue_kb,\\n       drs.redo_rate                   AS redo_rate_kb_per_sec,\\n       drs.is_suspended\\nFROM   sys.dm_hadr_database_replica_states drs\\nJOIN   sys.availability_replicas ar ON drs.replica_id = ar.replica_id\\nWHERE  ar.replica_server_name = '<returned_node_name>';\\n\\n-- Final AG health check\\nSELECT ag.name,\\n       ags.synchronization_health_desc,\\n       ags.primary_replica\\nFROM   sys.dm_hadr_availability_group_states ags\\nJOIN   sys.availability_groups ag ON ags.group_id = ag.group_id;", "parameters": {}, "description": "If databases are suspended after patching, resume them using ALTER DATABASE SET HADR RESUME on the primary. Monitor redo_queue_size until it reaches zero, indicating the secondary has caught up. Confirm the AG reports synchronization_health_desc = 'HEALTHY' before closing the incident."}	null	low	f	t	01:00:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.389673
2343	sqlserver	verify	Confirm instance is at expected pre-patch version before retrying	{"sql": "-- Confirm current version is exactly the pre-patch baseline (no partial state)\\nSELECT\\n  SERVERPROPERTY('ProductVersion') AS product_version,\\n  SERVERPROPERTY('ProductLevel') AS product_level,\\n  SERVERPROPERTY('ProductUpdateLevel') AS cu_level,\\n  sqlserver_start_time,\\n  DATEDIFF(hour, sqlserver_start_time, GETDATE()) AS hours_since_restart\\nFROM sys.dm_os_sys_info;\\n\\n-- Confirm no databases are stuck in non-ONLINE state\\nSELECT name, state_desc FROM sys.databases WHERE state_desc != 'ONLINE';\\n\\n-- Confirm no active long-running transactions that should be drained first\\nSELECT COUNT(*) AS active_user_sessions\\nFROM sys.dm_exec_sessions\\nWHERE is_user_process = 1 AND status != 'sleeping'", "parameters": {}, "description": "Verify the instance is in a clean pre-patch state with no lingering artifacts from the failed download attempt. All databases should be ONLINE, and the version should match the expected pre-patch baseline. If a restart is needed to clear a partial state, perform it before proceeding."}	null	low	f	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.389674
2317	sqlserver	verify	Confirm version uniformity and full AG health across all replicas	{"sql": "-- Verify all replicas show the same version\\nSELECT ar.replica_server_name,\\n       ars.role_desc,\\n       ars.connected_state_desc,\\n       ars.synchronization_health_desc\\nFROM   sys.dm_hadr_availability_replica_states ars\\nJOIN   sys.availability_replicas ar ON ars.replica_id = ar.replica_id;\\n\\n-- Overall AG health\\nSELECT ag.name,\\n       ags.synchronization_health_desc,\\n       ags.primary_replica\\nFROM   sys.dm_hadr_availability_group_states ags\\nJOIN   sys.availability_groups ag ON ags.group_id = ag.group_id;\\n\\n-- Verify no databases remain suspended\\nSELECT ar.replica_server_name,\\n       DB_NAME(drs.database_id) AS database_name,\\n       drs.synchronization_state_desc,\\n       drs.is_suspended\\nFROM   sys.dm_hadr_database_replica_states drs\\nJOIN   sys.availability_replicas ar ON drs.replica_id = ar.replica_id\\nWHERE  drs.is_suspended = 1;", "parameters": {}, "description": "Verify every replica reports the same ProductVersion value, all replicas are CONNECTED, and no databases are suspended. The AG group should report synchronization_health_desc = 'HEALTHY'. Document the final version matrix and the rollback decision in the incident ticket."}	null	low	f	t	00:10:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.389675
2320	sqlserver	verify	Apply missing CU to lagging nodes and confirm AG version consistency	{"sql": "-- Post-patch: confirm all replicas report the same build\\nSELECT ar.replica_server_name,\\n       ars.role_desc,\\n       ars.connected_state_desc,\\n       ars.synchronization_health_desc,\\n       SERVERPROPERTY('ProductVersion')     AS local_version,\\n       SERVERPROPERTY('ProductUpdateLevel') AS local_cu\\nFROM   sys.dm_hadr_availability_replica_states ars\\nJOIN   sys.availability_replicas ar ON ars.replica_id = ar.replica_id;\\n\\n-- Confirm no databases are suspended\\nSELECT ar.replica_server_name,\\n       DB_NAME(drs.database_id) AS database_name,\\n       drs.synchronization_state_desc,\\n       drs.is_suspended\\nFROM   sys.dm_hadr_database_replica_states drs\\nJOIN   sys.availability_replicas ar ON drs.replica_id = ar.replica_id\\nWHERE  drs.is_suspended = 1;", "parameters": {}, "description": "Using the now-standardized mechanism, apply the target CU to any node still below the required build (patch secondaries first, then fail over and patch the primary). After all patches are applied, run the SQL to confirm version consistency and full AG health."}	null	medium	f	t	02:00:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.389677
2321	sqlserver	verify	Quantify disk space deficit and identify reclaimable space	{"sql": "-- Identify volumes with low free space hosting SQL Server files\\nSELECT DISTINCT\\n       vs.volume_mount_point,\\n       vs.logical_volume_name,\\n       vs.total_bytes / 1073741824    AS total_gb,\\n       vs.available_bytes / 1073741824 AS available_gb,\\n       CAST(100.0 * vs.available_bytes / NULLIF(vs.total_bytes, 0) AS DECIMAL(5,1)) AS pct_free\\nFROM   sys.master_files mf\\nCROSS  APPLY sys.dm_os_volume_stats(mf.database_id, mf.file_id) vs\\nORDER  BY available_gb ASC;\\n\\n-- Check error log for the setup failure reason\\nCREATE TABLE #log (LogDate DATETIME, ProcessInfo VARCHAR(64), Text NVARCHAR(MAX));\\nINSERT INTO #log EXEC xp_readerrorlog 0, 1, N'disk';\\nINSERT INTO #log EXEC xp_readerrorlog 0, 1, N'space';\\nSELECT LogDate, Text FROM #log\\nWHERE  LogDate > DATEADD(day, -7, GETDATE())\\nORDER  BY LogDate DESC;\\nDROP TABLE #log;", "parameters": {}, "description": "Determine which volume is below the threshold needed for the CU installer (typically at least 3-5 GB on the system drive and on the SQL Server binary volume). On Windows, also check: Get-WmiObject Win32_LogicalDisk | Select DeviceID, FreeSpace, Size and review the setup bootstrap log for the specific disk space error."}	null	low	f	t	00:10:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.389679
2323	sqlserver	verify	Retry CU installation and confirm node rejoins AG at the correct build	{"sql": "-- Confirm disk space is now sufficient\\nSELECT DISTINCT\\n       vs.volume_mount_point,\\n       vs.available_bytes / 1073741824 AS available_gb\\nFROM   sys.master_files mf\\nCROSS  APPLY sys.dm_os_volume_stats(mf.database_id, mf.file_id) vs\\nORDER  BY available_gb ASC;\\n\\n-- After patch completes, confirm version and AG health\\nSELECT SERVERPROPERTY('ProductVersion')   AS new_version,\\n       SERVERPROPERTY('ProductUpdateLevel') AS new_cu;\\n\\nSELECT ar.replica_server_name,\\n       ars.connected_state_desc,\\n       ars.synchronization_health_desc,\\n       drs.synchronization_state_desc\\nFROM   sys.dm_hadr_availability_replica_states ars\\nJOIN   sys.availability_replicas ar ON ars.replica_id = ar.replica_id\\nLEFT   JOIN sys.dm_hadr_database_replica_states drs ON ars.replica_id = drs.replica_id\\nWHERE  ar.replica_server_name = SERVERPROPERTY('ServerName');", "parameters": {}, "description": "Verify disk space is now above the minimum threshold, then re-run the CU installer:\\n  SQLServer<version>-KB<number>-x64.exe /quiet /action=patch /instancename=MSSQLSERVER /IAcceptSQLServerLicenseTerms\\nAfter installation completes and the SQL Server service restarts, run the SQL above to confirm the new build matches the target and that this replica has reconnected to the AG."}	null	medium	t	t	00:45:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.38968
2324	sqlserver	verify	Inventory component versions and identify mismatches	{"sql": "-- Engine version and CU level\\nSELECT SERVERPROPERTY('ProductVersion')   AS engine_version,\\n       SERVERPROPERTY('ProductUpdateLevel') AS cu_level,\\n       SERVERPROPERTY('ProductLevel')       AS product_level,\\n       @@VERSION                            AS full_version_string;\\n\\n-- Check registry for installed components and their versions\\nSELECT registry_key, value_name, value_data\\nFROM   sys.dm_server_registry\\nWHERE  registry_key LIKE '%CurrentVersion%'\\n    OR registry_key LIKE '%Setup%'\\nORDER  BY registry_key, value_name;\\n\\n-- Check database compatibility levels (may indicate stale metadata)\\nSELECT name,\\n       compatibility_level,\\n       state_desc,\\n       is_read_only,\\n       is_auto_update_stats_on\\nFROM   sys.databases\\nWHERE  database_id > 4 AND state = 0\\nORDER  BY compatibility_level;", "parameters": {}, "description": "Run on each AG node. Also on Windows, check installed programs: Get-WmiObject Win32_Product | Where { $_.Name -like '*SQL Server*' } | Select Name, Version | Sort-Object Name. Build a component-version matrix for each node to identify exactly which components are at the wrong build."}	null	low	f	t	00:15:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.38968
