2641	sqlserver	verify	Confirm scope-leaked sessions and identify owning application	{"sql": "SELECT s.program_name, s.host_name, s.login_name,\\n  COUNT(*) AS leaked_sessions,\\n  AVG(DATEDIFF(MINUTE, s.last_request_end_time, GETDATE())) AS avg_idle_min,\\n  AVG(DATEDIFF(SECOND, s.last_request_start_time, s.last_request_end_time)) AS avg_req_duration_sec,\\n  SUM(s.open_transaction_count) AS total_open_txns\\nFROM sys.dm_exec_sessions s\\nJOIN sys.dm_exec_connections c ON s.session_id = c.session_id\\nWHERE s.status = 'sleeping'\\n  AND s.is_user_process = 1\\n  AND DATEDIFF(MINUTE, s.last_request_end_time, GETDATE()) > 30\\n  AND DATEDIFF(SECOND, s.last_request_start_time, s.last_request_end_time) < 5\\nGROUP BY s.program_name, s.host_name, s.login_name\\nHAVING COUNT(*) > 5\\nORDER BY leaked_sessions DESC;", "description": "Confirms which application programs are leaking connections across scopes and how many sessions are affected. Output identifies the primary offenders for escalation."}	{"description": "Read-only verification step; no rollback needed."}	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.453378
2642	sqlserver	instruct	Instruct application team to audit child thread connection patterns	{"parameters": {"urgency": "High — connection pool exhaustion risk", "target_team": "Application development", "pattern_to_eliminate": "Passing open SqlConnection across async scope boundaries"}, "description": "Escalate findings to the application development team. They must audit all async/background task patterns for the identified program_name. Key code patterns to fix: (1) Ensure SqlConnection is declared with 'using' blocks within each request scope. (2) Never pass a SqlConnection object to a Task.Run(), ThreadPool, or async void method without ensuring the calling scope outlives all consumers. (3) Use connection-per-task pattern for parallel work: each Task creates, uses, and disposes its own connection. (4) For child threads, pass the connection string, not the open connection object. Example fix: Replace 'Task.Run(() => DoWork(openConn))' with 'Task.Run(() => { using (var conn = new SqlConnection(connStr)) { conn.Open(); DoWork(conn); } })'."}	{"description": "No server-side change; application code change can be reverted via deployment rollback."}	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.453381
