2660	sqlserver	instruct	Deploy connection proxy layer for serverless workloads	{"parameters": {"aws_option": "RDS Proxy (SQL Server supported)", "azure_option": "Azure SQL built-in pooling or RDS Proxy", "on_prem_option": "Static connection in function warm path or HAProxy TCP passthrough", "recommended_pool_size_for_proxy": "20-50 connections to SQL Server from proxy"}, "description": "Choose and deploy a connection pooling proxy appropriate for the environment: (1) Azure SQL / SQL Server on Azure: Use Azure SQL Database connection pooling (built-in) or Azure Application Gateway with SQL proxy. For Azure Functions specifically, use 'SQL Connection Resiliency' and static SqlConnection instances with SqlConnectionStringBuilder. (2) AWS RDS SQL Server: Use RDS Proxy with SQL Server support for Lambda functions. (3) On-premises / self-hosted: Deploy PgBouncer-equivalent for SQL Server using SQL Proxy, ProxySQL (limited SQL Server support), or HAProxy with TCP passthrough combined with application-level pooling (Hikari in a long-running process). (4) For Lambda/Cloud Functions specifically: Refactor the function to use a warm connection pattern — initialize SqlConnection as a static/module-level variable outside the handler function. This reuses the connection across invocations in the same execution environment."}	{"description": "Revert application connection strings to point directly at SQL Server and decommission the proxy."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.453389
2661	sqlserver	configure	Configure SQL Server login for proxy service account with appropriate permissions	{"sql": "-- Create a dedicated login for the connection proxy if not already existing\\n-- Replace values as appropriate\\nIF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sys.server_principals WHERE name = 'svc_proxy')\\nBEGIN\\n    CREATE LOGIN [svc_proxy] WITH PASSWORD = 'StrongPassword123!',\\n      DEFAULT_DATABASE = [YourAppDB],\\n      CHECK_EXPIRATION = ON,\\n      CHECK_POLICY = ON;\\nEND;\\n\\n-- Create database user for proxy login\\nUSE [YourAppDB];\\nIF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sys.database_principals WHERE name = 'svc_proxy')\\nBEGIN\\n    CREATE USER [svc_proxy] FOR LOGIN [svc_proxy];\\n    ALTER ROLE db_datareader ADD MEMBER [svc_proxy];\\n    ALTER ROLE db_datawriter ADD MEMBER [svc_proxy];\\nEND;\\n\\n-- Verify proxy login exists and is enabled\\nSELECT name, type_desc, is_disabled, default_database_name\\nFROM sys.server_principals\\nWHERE name = 'svc_proxy';", "description": "Creates and configures a dedicated service account for the connection proxy. Using a separate login allows per-login connection throttling and auditing of proxy traffic."}	{"sql": "USE [YourAppDB];\\nDROP USER IF EXISTS [svc_proxy];\\nUSE master;\\nDROP LOGIN IF EXISTS [svc_proxy];", "description": "Removes the proxy service account login and database user."}	low	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.45339
