2666	sqlserver	verify	Confirm pool consolidated to single connection profile per application	{"sql": "-- Re-run after application restart\\nSELECT s.program_name, s.host_name,\\n  COUNT(DISTINCT s.login_name) AS distinct_logins,\\n  COUNT(DISTINCT DB_NAME(s.database_id)) AS distinct_databases,\\n  COUNT(DISTINCT c.encrypt_option) AS distinct_encrypt_options,\\n  COUNT(*) AS total_sessions\\nFROM sys.dm_exec_sessions s\\nJOIN sys.dm_exec_connections c ON s.session_id = c.session_id\\nWHERE s.is_user_process = 1\\nGROUP BY s.program_name, s.host_name\\nORDER BY total_sessions DESC;\\n\\n-- Success: distinct_logins = 1, distinct_databases = 1 per program_name + host", "description": "Verifies that each application now uses exactly one login and one database in its connection pool. Multiple distinct logins or databases per application still indicate unfixed connection string variation."}	{"description": "Read-only verification; no rollback needed."}	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.453393
2667	sqlserver	verify	Quantify total connection count and distribution across backend instances	{"sql": "SELECT s.program_name,\\n  c.client_net_address,\\n  COUNT(*) AS sessions_from_host,\\n  SUM(CASE WHEN s.status = 'sleeping' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS sleeping,\\n  SUM(CASE WHEN s.status = 'running' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS running,\\n  AVG(DATEDIFF(SECOND, s.login_time, GETDATE())) AS avg_age_sec\\nFROM sys.dm_exec_sessions s\\nJOIN sys.dm_exec_connections c ON s.session_id = c.session_id\\nWHERE s.is_user_process = 1\\nGROUP BY s.program_name, c.client_net_address\\nORDER BY sessions_from_host DESC;\\n\\n-- Summary: total connections vs backend instance count\\nSELECT s.program_name,\\n  COUNT(DISTINCT c.client_net_address) AS backend_instances,\\n  COUNT(*) AS total_connections,\\n  COUNT(*) / NULLIF(COUNT(DISTINCT c.client_net_address), 0) AS connections_per_instance,\\n  SUM(CASE WHEN s.status = 'sleeping' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS total_sleeping\\nFROM sys.dm_exec_sessions s\\nJOIN sys.dm_exec_connections c ON s.session_id = c.session_id\\nWHERE s.is_user_process = 1\\nGROUP BY s.program_name;", "description": "Maps all backend instances and their connection counts. Identifies total connection pressure and the ratio of sleeping (idle pool) connections that could be consolidated."}	{"description": "Read-only verification; no rollback needed."}	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.453394
2674	sqlserver	verify	Confirm health check query execution count has decreased significantly	{"sql": "-- Clear plan cache to get fresh baseline (WARNING: clears all cached plans)\\n-- Only do this in a maintenance window: DBCC FREEPROCCACHE;\\n-- Instead, compare relative execution counts after waiting 5-10 minutes:\\nSELECT TOP 10\\n  qs.execution_count,\\n  SUBSTRING(qt.text, 1, 200) AS query_text\\nFROM sys.dm_exec_query_stats qs\\nCROSS APPLY sys.dm_exec_sql_text(qs.sql_handle) qt\\nWHERE (qt.text LIKE '%SELECT 1%'\\n  OR qt.text LIKE '%SELECT @@%'\\n  OR qt.text LIKE '%SELECT GETDATE%')\\nORDER BY qs.execution_count DESC;\\n\\n-- Verify connection reset rate has improved\\nSELECT cntr_value AS connection_resets_total\\nFROM sys.dm_os_performance_counters\\nWHERE object_name LIKE '%General Statistics%'\\n  AND counter_name = 'Connection Resets/sec';", "description": "Confirms that health check query execution counts are growing at a much slower rate after the configuration change. Connection resets should also be lower if testOnBorrow was generating resets."}	{"description": "Read-only verification; no rollback needed."}	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.453398
2668	sqlserver	instruct	Deploy centralized connection proxy appropriate for the environment	{"parameters": {"proxy_redundancy": "Deploy 2 proxy instances for HA with load balancer in front", "recommended_tools": "Azure SQL Gateway (Azure), RDS Proxy (AWS), Heimdall Data (on-prem SQL Server)", "target_proxy_pool_size": "50-100 connections (versus current N_instances * pool_size)"}, "description": "Choose a proxy approach based on infrastructure: (1) Azure SQL / SQL Managed Instance: Use Azure SQL Database built-in connection pooling with multiple backend instances pointing to the same connection string. Azure automatically pools connections at the gateway. (2) AWS RDS SQL Server: Use RDS Proxy. Configure the proxy endpoint and update all application connection strings to use the proxy DNS endpoint. Set proxy max connections to 50-100. (3) On-premises: Deploy a dedicated process that maintains a centralized SQLConnection pool and exposes an HTTP or TCP interface to backend instances, OR use a dedicated backend 'DB Broker' microservice that all instances call. (4) Kubernetes: Use a sidecar proxy pattern or a dedicated proxy Deployment with a fixed replica count, backed by a HPA-aware pool. Update all backend Deployments to inject the proxy service DNS as the DB host."}	{"description": "Revert all application connection strings to point directly at SQL Server and decommission proxy instances."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.453394
2702	sqlserver	verify	Confirm THREADPOOL waits cleared and session count stabilised below safe threshold	{"sql": "SELECT\\n  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM sys.dm_exec_sessions WHERE is_user_process = 1) AS current_user_sessions,\\n  (SELECT CAST(value_in_use AS INT) FROM sys.configurations WHERE name = 'max worker threads') - 96 AS safe_user_capacity,\\n  (SELECT waiting_tasks_count FROM sys.dm_os_wait_stats WHERE wait_type = 'THREADPOOL') AS threadpool_wait_tasks,\\n  (SELECT SUM(work_queue_count) FROM sys.dm_os_schedulers WHERE status = 'VISIBLE ONLINE') AS queued_tasks", "parameters": {}, "description": "Verify current_user_sessions < safe_user_capacity, THREADPOOL wait tasks = 0, and queued_tasks = 0. These confirm the server is no longer oversubscribed."}	null	low	f	t	00:10:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.457066
2669	sqlserver	configure	Set SQL Server max connections for per-application governance	{"sql": "-- Optionally use Resource Governor to limit connections per application\\n-- First check if Resource Governor is enabled\\nSELECT is_enabled FROM sys.resource_governor_configuration;\\n\\n-- If enabled, view existing pools and groups\\nSELECT pool_id, name, max_connections_per_session\\nFROM sys.dm_resource_governor_resource_pools;\\n\\n-- As a simpler alternative, set max connections at server level\\n-- to prevent runaway growth during proxy migration\\nSELECT name, value_in_use\\nFROM sys.configurations\\nWHERE name = 'max connections';\\n\\n-- Set a reasonable cap (default 32767, recommend 500 during migration)\\n-- EXEC sp_configure 'max connections', 500;\\n-- RECONFIGURE WITH OVERRIDE;", "description": "Reviews SQL Server connection governance options. Setting a temporary max connections cap during the proxy migration prevents runaway connection accumulation if the migration is staged."}	{"sql": "EXEC sp_configure 'max connections', 0;\\nRECONFIGURE WITH OVERRIDE;", "description": "Restore unlimited max connections (0 = SQL Server default)."}	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.453395
2670	sqlserver	verify	Confirm total connection count reduced and sleeping connections eliminated	{"sql": "-- Run after all backend instances are migrated to the proxy\\nSELECT s.program_name,\\n  COUNT(DISTINCT c.client_net_address) AS source_hosts,\\n  COUNT(*) AS total_connections,\\n  SUM(CASE WHEN s.status = 'sleeping' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS sleeping,\\n  SUM(CASE WHEN s.status = 'running' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS running\\nFROM sys.dm_exec_sessions s\\nJOIN sys.dm_exec_connections c ON s.session_id = c.session_id\\nWHERE s.is_user_process = 1\\nGROUP BY s.program_name\\nORDER BY total_connections DESC;\\n\\n-- Confirm source hosts are now proxy IPs (not backend instance IPs)\\nSELECT DISTINCT c.client_net_address\\nFROM sys.dm_exec_sessions s\\nJOIN sys.dm_exec_connections c ON s.session_id = c.session_id\\nWHERE s.is_user_process = 1\\n  AND s.login_name = 'svc_app'; -- replace with actual login", "description": "Verifies that SQL Server now receives connections only from proxy IP addresses (not individual backend instance IPs), and that total connection count has decreased significantly."}	{"description": "Read-only verification; no rollback needed."}	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.453395
2671	sqlserver	verify	Confirm health check queries dominate plan cache by execution count	{"sql": "SELECT TOP 20\\n  qs.execution_count,\\n  qs.total_worker_time / qs.execution_count AS avg_cpu_us,\\n  qs.total_elapsed_time / qs.execution_count AS avg_elapsed_us,\\n  SUBSTRING(qt.text, 1, 200) AS query_text\\nFROM sys.dm_exec_query_stats qs\\nCROSS APPLY sys.dm_exec_sql_text(qs.sql_handle) qt\\nWHERE qt.text NOT LIKE '%dm_exec%'\\n  AND qt.text NOT LIKE '%sys.%'\\nORDER BY qs.execution_count DESC;\\n\\n-- Also check sp_reset_connection frequency\\nSELECT\\n  (SELECT cntr_value FROM sys.dm_os_performance_counters\\n   WHERE object_name LIKE '%General Statistics%' AND counter_name = 'Connection Resets/sec') AS connection_resets,\\n  (SELECT cntr_value FROM sys.dm_os_performance_counters\\n   WHERE object_name LIKE '%General Statistics%' AND counter_name = 'Logins/sec') AS logins_sec;", "description": "Identifies if trivial health check queries (SELECT 1, SELECT GETDATE(), etc.) have disproportionately high execution counts compared to actual application queries. Connection resets much higher than logins indicates aggressive pool validation."}	{"description": "Read-only verification; no rollback needed."}	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.453396
2672	sqlserver	instruct	Reduce health check frequency and disable testOnBorrow in pool configuration	{"parameters": {"adonet_note": "ADO.NET SQL Client does not need a validation query; remove any SELECT 1 ping logic", "disable_testOnBorrow": "true", "recommended_keepalive_ms": "600000 (10 minutes)", "preferred_validation_strategy": "testWhileIdle every 5 minutes"}, "description": "Update the connection pool configuration to reduce health check aggressiveness: (1) HikariCP: Set keepaliveTime=600000 (10 min, not 30s), connectionTestQuery should not be set (HikariCP uses JDBC4 isValid() which is cheaper). Remove testOnBorrow=true if present. Set idleTimeout=600000 and maxLifetime=1800000. (2) DBCP2/Commons Pool: Set validationQuery='SELECT 1', testOnBorrow=false, testWhileIdle=true, timeBetweenEvictionRunsMillis=300000 (5 min), validationQueryTimeout=5. (3) c3p0: Set preferredTestQuery='SELECT 1', testConnectionOnCheckout=false, testConnectionOnCheckin=false, idleConnectionTestPeriod=300 (5 min), testConnectionOnCheckin=false. Key principle: test connections on return or periodically while idle — NOT on every borrow. For ADO.NET (SQL Client), connection health is verified transparently; no manual health check query is needed."}	{"description": "Restore previous pool configuration values and redeploy."}	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.453397
2673	sqlserver	configure	Optimize SQL Server for connection reuse by disabling unnecessary session resets	{"sql": "-- SQL Server automatically runs sp_reset_connection when connections are reused from pool.\\n-- This is not configurable but is efficient by default.\\n-- If the application is running a manual ping query (SELECT 1), advise removing it.\\n-- Check if there are any session-level SET options being changed on each borrow:\\nSELECT TOP 20\\n  qs.execution_count,\\n  SUBSTRING(qt.text, 1, 300) AS query_text\\nFROM sys.dm_exec_query_stats qs\\nCROSS APPLY sys.dm_exec_sql_text(qs.sql_handle) qt\\nWHERE (qt.text LIKE '%SET ARITHABORT%'\\n  OR qt.text LIKE '%SET NOCOUNT%'\\n  OR qt.text LIKE '%SET ANSI_NULLS%'\\n  OR qt.text LIKE '%SET TRANSACTION ISOLATION%')\\nORDER BY qs.execution_count DESC;\\n-- If SET options appear with high execution counts, the pool resets these on each borrow.\\n-- Ensure the connection string specifies them once (e.g., in 'Initial SET' options) rather than per-request.", "description": "Checks whether session-level SET options are being applied on each connection borrow, which adds overhead on top of sp_reset_connection. If found, these should be set once in the connection setup, not per-request."}	{"description": "No server-side change in this step; application-level adjustment only."}	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.453398
2680	sqlserver	instruct	Increase driver timeout settings in connection string and pool configuration	{"parameters": {"hikari_idle_timeout": "idleTimeout=600000 (10 minutes minimum)", "jdbc_socket_timeout": "socketTimeout=300000 (5 minutes)", "ado_net_critical_fix": "Connection Lifetime=0 (disable) and Load Balance Timeout=0 (disable)", "ado_net_connect_timeout": "Connect Timeout=30"}, "description": "Update the connection string and pool configuration to use appropriate driver timeout values. Key settings per driver: (1) ADO.NET (System.Data.SqlClient / Microsoft.Data.SqlClient): 'Connect Timeout=30' (default is 15s — increase to 30s for high-latency networks). 'Connection Lifetime=0' (IMPORTANT: set to 0 to disable ADO.NET's built-in connection lifetime — values like 60 cause connections older than 60s to be destroyed on return to pool, causing massive churn). 'Load Balance Timeout=0' (same as Connection Lifetime; set to 0). (2) JDBC mssql-jdbc: 'loginTimeout=30', 'socketTimeout=300000' (5 min — prevents stuck connections, not premature closure). Do NOT set 'connectionTimeout' too low. (3) HikariCP: 'connectionTimeout=30000' (30s — time to wait for a pool connection, not close idle ones). 'idleTimeout=600000' (10 min minimum)."}	{"description": "Restore previous connection string timeout values and redeploy application."}	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.455889
