3237	sqlserver	verify	Re-check index usage after rebuild	{"sql": "-- Check usage stats 24-48 hours after the rebuild.\\nSELECT i.name                               AS index_name,\\n       ISNULL(ius.user_seeks,  0)           AS user_seeks,\\n       ISNULL(ius.user_scans,  0)           AS user_scans,\\n       ISNULL(ius.user_updates,0)           AS user_updates,\\n       ISNULL(ius.last_user_seek, ius.last_user_scan) AS last_used\\nFROM sys.indexes i\\nLEFT JOIN sys.dm_db_index_usage_stats ius\\n       ON i.object_id  = ius.object_id\\n      AND i.index_id   = ius.index_id\\n      AND ius.database_id = DB_ID()\\nWHERE i.object_id = OBJECT_ID('<schema>.<table_name>')\\n  AND i.type > 0\\nORDER BY i.index_id;", "parameters": {}, "description": "After the rebuild, confirms whether the optimizer has begun using the index. If seeks/scans remain zero after 48 hours of normal workload, the index should be dropped."}	null	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.525882
2699	sqlserver	verify	Confirm login rate and very-new-connection count have dropped	{"sql": "SELECT\\n  (SELECT cntr_value FROM sys.dm_os_performance_counters\\n   WHERE counter_name = 'Logins/sec'\\n     AND object_name LIKE '%General Statistics%') AS logins_sec,\\n  (SELECT cntr_value FROM sys.dm_os_performance_counters\\n   WHERE counter_name = 'Connection Resets/sec'\\n     AND object_name LIKE '%General Statistics%') AS connection_resets_sec,\\n  SUM(CASE WHEN DATEDIFF(SECOND, c.connect_time, GETDATE()) < 10 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS very_new_connections\\nFROM sys.dm_exec_connections c", "parameters": {}, "description": "Logins/sec should drop to near zero (only new pool initialisation). Very new connections (<10s) should be minimal. Connection Resets/sec (pool reuse) should remain healthy."}	null	low	f	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.457064
