3817	sqlserver	verify	Identify overestimating queries with subquery patterns	{"sql": "SELECT TOP 10\\n  qs.query_hash,\\n  qs.execution_count,\\n  qs.max_grant_kb / 1024 AS max_grant_mb,\\n  qs.max_used_grant_kb / 1024 AS max_used_mb,\\n  CAST(qs.max_used_grant_kb AS FLOAT) / NULLIF(qs.max_grant_kb, 0) * 100 AS pct_used,\\n  SUBSTRING(t.text, (qs.statement_start_offset/2)+1, 300) AS query_fragment\\nFROM sys.dm_exec_query_stats qs\\nCROSS APPLY sys.dm_exec_sql_text(qs.sql_handle) t\\nWHERE qs.max_grant_kb > 51200\\n  AND qs.max_used_grant_kb < qs.max_grant_kb * 0.20\\n  AND (t.text LIKE '%SELECT%FROM%(%SELECT%FROM%' OR t.text LIKE '%IN%(%SELECT%' OR t.text LIKE '%EXISTS%(%SELECT%')\\nORDER BY qs.max_grant_kb DESC;", "parameters": [], "description": "Finds queries with subquery patterns (IN, EXISTS, derived tables) that have severely overestimated memory grants."}	null	low	f	t	00:01:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.579283
3818	sqlserver	instruct	Rewrite subqueries as explicit JOINs with proper filtering	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "For each identified subquery pattern: (1) IN subquery => INNER JOIN: Replace WHERE col IN (SELECT col FROM sub) with INNER JOIN sub ON main.col = sub.col. (2) NOT IN => LEFT JOIN/IS NULL: Replace WHERE col NOT IN (SELECT ...) with LEFT JOIN ... WHERE sub.col IS NULL (handles NULLs correctly). (3) EXISTS => INNER JOIN or CROSS APPLY: Replace WHERE EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sub WHERE sub.col = main.col) with CROSS APPLY or INNER JOIN. (4) Scalar subquery in SELECT => OUTER APPLY: Replace (SELECT MAX(col) FROM sub WHERE ...) with OUTER APPLY. (5) Ensure all JOINs have proper ON conditions with selective predicates."}	null	low	f	t	5 days	2026-02-24 13:10:27.579284
