3868	sqlserver	verify	Identify skewed columns in parallel queries	{"sql": "SELECT TOP 10\\n  qs.query_hash,\\n  qs.total_elapsed_time / qs.execution_count AS avg_elapsed_us,\\n  qs.total_worker_time / qs.execution_count AS avg_cpu_us,\\n  CAST(qs.total_worker_time AS FLOAT) / NULLIF(qs.total_elapsed_time, 0) AS cpu_efficiency,\\n  qs.execution_count,\\n  SUBSTRING(t.text, (qs.statement_start_offset/2)+1, 300) AS query_fragment\\nFROM sys.dm_exec_query_stats qs\\nCROSS APPLY sys.dm_exec_sql_text(qs.sql_handle) t\\nWHERE qs.total_worker_time / NULLIF(qs.execution_count, 0) > 0\\n  AND (qs.total_elapsed_time - qs.total_worker_time) > qs.total_worker_time * 0.5\\n  AND qs.execution_count > 5\\nORDER BY qs.total_elapsed_time DESC;", "parameters": [], "description": "Finds parallel queries where elapsed time greatly exceeds CPU time, indicating thread imbalance (one thread works while others wait on CXPACKET)."}	null	low	f	t	00:01:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.579315
3869	sqlserver	execute	Update statistics and create filtered stats for skewed columns	{"sql": "-- Update statistics with FULLSCAN on tables used by imbalanced queries\\nUPDATE STATISTICS [@schema_name].[@table_name] WITH FULLSCAN;\\n\\n-- Create filtered statistics for the dominant value\\n-- CREATE STATISTICS [STAT_filtered_dominant_value]\\n--   ON [schema].[table] (join_column)\\n--   WHERE status_column = 'dominant_value'\\n--   WITH FULLSCAN;", "parameters": ["schema_name", "table_name"], "description": "Updates statistics with FULLSCAN and creates filtered statistics for dominant values that cause skew. DBA identifies the specific skewed columns from the query plans."}	null	low	t	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.579316
3870	sqlserver	verify	Verify improved parallel efficiency	{"sql": "SELECT TOP 10\\n  qs.query_hash,\\n  qs.total_elapsed_time / qs.execution_count AS avg_elapsed_us,\\n  qs.total_worker_time / qs.execution_count AS avg_cpu_us,\\n  CAST(qs.total_worker_time AS FLOAT) / NULLIF(qs.total_elapsed_time, 0) AS cpu_efficiency\\nFROM sys.dm_exec_query_stats qs\\nWHERE qs.execution_count > 5\\nORDER BY qs.total_elapsed_time DESC;", "parameters": [], "description": "Checks that CPU efficiency has improved (closer to 1.0) for the previously imbalanced queries."}	null	low	f	t	00:01:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.579317
3871	sqlserver	verify	Assess partition row distribution skew	{"sql": "SELECT\\n  OBJECT_SCHEMA_NAME(p.object_id) + '.' + OBJECT_NAME(p.object_id) AS table_name,\\n  p.partition_number,\\n  p.rows,\\n  CAST(p.rows AS FLOAT) / NULLIF(SUM(p.rows) OVER (PARTITION BY p.object_id), 0) * 100 AS pct_of_total,\\n  COUNT(*) OVER (PARTITION BY p.object_id) AS partition_count\\nFROM sys.partitions p\\nWHERE p.index_id IN (0, 1)\\n  AND p.rows > 0\\n  AND (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM sys.partitions p2 WHERE p2.object_id = p.object_id AND p2.index_id = p.index_id AND p2.rows > 0) > 1\\nORDER BY p.object_id, p.partition_number;", "parameters": [], "description": "Shows row distribution across partitions to identify skew. A single partition holding >50% of rows causes significant thread imbalance."}	null	low	f	t	00:01:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.579318
3873	sqlserver	verify	Verify improved parallel balance on partitioned tables	{"sql": "SELECT TOP 10\\n  qs.query_hash,\\n  qs.total_elapsed_time / qs.execution_count AS avg_elapsed_us,\\n  qs.total_worker_time / qs.execution_count AS avg_cpu_us,\\n  CAST(qs.total_worker_time AS FLOAT) / NULLIF(qs.total_elapsed_time, 0) AS cpu_efficiency\\nFROM sys.dm_exec_query_stats qs\\nCROSS APPLY sys.dm_exec_query_plan(qs.plan_handle) qp\\nWHERE qp.query_plan.exist('//RelOp[@PhysicalOp=\\"Parallelism\\"]') = 1\\n  AND qs.execution_count > 5\\nORDER BY qs.total_elapsed_time DESC;", "parameters": [], "description": "Checks CPU efficiency for parallel queries on partitioned tables after optimization."}	null	low	f	t	00:01:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.579319
3874	sqlserver	verify	Identify hash join queries with thread imbalance	{"sql": "SELECT TOP 10\\n  qs.query_hash,\\n  qs.total_elapsed_time / qs.execution_count AS avg_elapsed_us,\\n  qs.total_worker_time / qs.execution_count AS avg_cpu_us,\\n  CAST(qs.total_worker_time AS FLOAT) / NULLIF(qs.total_elapsed_time, 0) AS cpu_efficiency,\\n  qs.execution_count,\\n  SUBSTRING(t.text, (qs.statement_start_offset/2)+1, 300) AS query_fragment\\nFROM sys.dm_exec_query_stats qs\\nCROSS APPLY sys.dm_exec_sql_text(qs.sql_handle) t\\nCROSS APPLY sys.dm_exec_query_plan(qs.plan_handle) qp\\nWHERE qp.query_plan.exist('//RelOp[@PhysicalOp=\\"Hash Match\\"]') = 1\\n  AND qp.query_plan.exist('//RelOp[@PhysicalOp=\\"Parallelism\\"]') = 1\\n  AND CAST(qs.total_worker_time AS FLOAT) / NULLIF(qs.total_elapsed_time, 0) < 0.5\\n  AND qs.execution_count > 5\\nORDER BY qs.total_elapsed_time DESC;", "parameters": [], "description": "Finds parallel hash join queries with poor CPU efficiency (elapsed >> CPU), indicating thread imbalance from hash collisions."}	null	low	f	t	00:01:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.57932
3875	sqlserver	instruct	Rewrite queries or apply hints to avoid skewed hash distribution	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "Options to fix hash collision imbalance: (1) Add OPTION (MERGE JOIN) or OPTION (LOOP JOIN) hints to force a different join strategy. (2) Add more columns to the JOIN condition if semantically correct (more columns = better hash distribution). (3) Pre-aggregate the skewed side before joining to reduce the cardinality of the problem column. (4) For GROUP BY on low-cardinality columns, filter out the dominant value and process separately. (5) Update statistics with FULLSCAN on the join columns to give the optimizer better distribution information. (6) Consider adding OPTION (MAXDOP 1) for queries where serial execution is faster than imbalanced parallel."}	null	low	f	t	5 days	2026-02-24 13:10:27.579321
