3999	sqlserver	instruct	Add upper bounds and optimize range queries	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "For each open-ended range query: (1) Add upper bound where business logic allows (WHERE date_col > @start AND date_col < @end instead of WHERE date_col > @start). (2) Use BETWEEN for bounded ranges (WHERE date_col BETWEEN @start AND @end). (3) For pagination, use keyset pagination (WHERE id > @last_id ORDER BY id FETCH FIRST 100) instead of OFFSET/FETCH. (4) Update statistics with FULLSCAN on range columns so the optimizer accurately estimates the range selectivity. (5) If the range typically returns <30% of the table, ensure an index exists on the range column."}	null	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.608324
