4331	sqlserver	instruct	Implement compensating controls for legacy application logins	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["legacy_app_name", "allowed_ip_addresses"], "description": "For legacy applications that cannot handle complex passwords: (1) Create a DEDICATED login for each legacy app (never share logins across applications). (2) Grant MINIMUM required database permissions only -- never sysadmin. (3) Restrict the login to specific databases only: ALTER LOGIN [legacy_app] WITH DEFAULT_DATABASE = [app_db]; DENY CONNECT SQL TO [legacy_app] -- then grant only via database-level. (4) Implement network-level restrictions: create a logon trigger that allows the legacy login only from specific IP addresses. (5) Enable CHECK_POLICY = ON even for legacy apps. If the password complexity is the issue, set a LONG password (20+ chars) of only lowercase letters -- this often satisfies both policy and legacy app requirements. (6) Document each exception with a security waiver and remediation timeline."}	null	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.713241
