4336	sqlserver	instruct	Configure Windows Local Security Policy for passphrase requirements	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "Configure the Windows Local Security Policy on the SQL Server host to enforce passphrase-friendly requirements: (1) Open Local Security Policy (secpol.msc) or Group Policy Management. (2) Navigate to Account Policies > Password Policy. (3) Set Minimum password length: 14 characters (enables passphrases). (4) Set Password complexity requirements: Enabled (requires 3 of 4 character classes). (5) Set Enforce password history: 12 passwords remembered. (6) Set Maximum password age: 365 days (NIST-aligned long rotation). (7) Set Minimum password age: 1 day (prevents rapid cycling). SQL Server's CHECK_POLICY will enforce these settings for all SQL logins with is_policy_checked = 1."}	null	low	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.716471
