4439	sqlserver	instruct	Remediate each development-style configuration in production	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "Systematically harden each finding from step 1: (1) Replace empty/weak passwords with strong credentials: ALTER LOGIN [name] WITH PASSWORD = N'<strong_password>', CHECK_POLICY = ON. (2) Disable guest access in user databases: REVOKE CONNECT FROM guest. (3) Disable sa: ALTER LOGIN sa DISABLE. (4) Disable remote DAC if not needed: EXEC sp_configure 'remote admin connections', 0; RECONFIGURE. (5) Disable xp_cmdshell: EXEC sp_configure 'xp_cmdshell', 0; RECONFIGURE. (6) Update all application connection strings with new credentials. (7) Implement a configuration management check to prevent future dev-to-prod drift."}	null	medium	t	t	04:00:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.750976
