4617	sqlserver	verify	Assess current direct-grant vs role-grant ratio	{"sql": "SELECT\\n  SUM(CASE WHEN dp.type_desc IN ('SQL_USER', 'WINDOWS_USER', 'EXTERNAL_USER') THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS direct_user_grants,\\n  SUM(CASE WHEN dp.type_desc = 'DATABASE_ROLE' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS role_grants,\\n  COUNT(*) AS total_grants\\nFROM sys.database_permissions p\\nJOIN sys.database_principals dp ON p.grantee_principal_id = dp.principal_id\\nWHERE p.state_desc IN ('GRANT', 'GRANT_WITH_GRANT_OPTION')\\n  AND p.class_desc <> 'DATABASE'\\n  AND dp.principal_id > 4;", "parameters": [], "description": "Measures the ratio of direct user grants vs role-based grants. High direct_user_grants indicates lack of RBAC."}	null	low	f	t	00:01:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.751087
4618	sqlserver	instruct	Design and create custom roles matching job functions	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "Design an RBAC model: (1) Identify distinct job functions that need database access (analyst, application_user, developer, report_runner, etl_user). (2) For each function, determine the minimum set of permissions required. (3) Create custom database roles for each function: CREATE ROLE [role_analyst]; CREATE ROLE [role_app_user]; etc. (4) Grant specific permissions to each role (not db_owner or db_datareader for granularity). (5) Migrate users from direct grants to role membership: ALTER ROLE [role_analyst] ADD MEMBER [username]; (6) Revoke the previous direct grants after verifying role-based access works. (7) Document role definitions, permission sets, and role assignment procedures."}	null	medium	t	t	5 days	2026-02-24 13:10:27.751088
