4624	sqlserver	instruct	Create production permission standards and deploy least-privilege accounts	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "Implement environment-specific permission standards: (1) Document the minimum permissions each application needs in production using sp_addrolemember and GRANT statements. (2) Create production-specific database roles with only the required permissions. (3) Create separate production service accounts that are NOT sysadmin. (4) For each application, run the application against a test database with the restricted permissions to identify any permission errors. (5) Fix any permission errors by adding specific GRANT statements rather than elevating to db_owner/sysadmin. (6) Add a deployment checklist step that verifies production accounts are not over-privileged. (7) Block sysadmin usage in production for non-DBA accounts via policy."}	null	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.765175
