4734	sqlserver	instruct	Implement cross-database orphan monitoring and environment-specific cleanup schedules	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "Create comprehensive orphan management: (1) Create a SQL Agent job that iterates all user databases and checks for orphaned users using sp_MSforeachdb. (2) Store results in a central tracking table. (3) Prioritize production databases for immediate cleanup. (4) Schedule development/staging cleanup on a monthly cadence. (5) For each environment: transfer schema ownership of orphaned users to dbo, then drop the user. (6) Disable or drop logins that have no mapped users in any database. (7) Send weekly summary reports to the DBA team. (8) Track orphan count trends over time to measure improvement."}	null	low	f	t	04:00:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.788693
