4739	sqlserver	verify	Find default application accounts with unchanged passwords	{"sql": "SELECT sp.name AS login_name, sp.type_desc,\\n  sp.create_date, sp.modify_date,\\n  CASE WHEN sp.create_date = sp.modify_date THEN 'NEVER_MODIFIED' ELSE 'MODIFIED' END AS modification_status,\\n  CASE WHEN CAST(LOGINPROPERTY(sp.name, 'PasswordLastSetTime') AS DATETIME) = sp.create_date\\n    THEN 'DEFAULT_PASSWORD' ELSE 'CHANGED' END AS password_status,\\n  STRING_AGG(sr.name, ', ') AS server_roles\\nFROM sys.server_principals sp\\nJOIN sys.sql_logins sl ON sp.principal_id = sl.principal_id\\nLEFT JOIN sys.server_role_members srm ON sp.principal_id = srm.member_principal_id\\nLEFT JOIN sys.server_principals sr ON srm.role_principal_id = sr.principal_id AND sr.type = 'R'\\nWHERE sp.is_disabled = 0 AND sp.name NOT LIKE '##%'\\n  AND (sp.name LIKE '%app%' OR sp.name LIKE '%svc%' OR sp.name LIKE '%service%'\\n    OR sp.name LIKE '%default%' OR sp.name LIKE '%webapp%' OR sp.name LIKE '%api%')\\n  AND (sp.create_date = sp.modify_date OR CAST(LOGINPROPERTY(sp.name, 'PasswordLastSetTime') AS DATETIME) = sp.create_date)\\nGROUP BY sp.name, sp.type_desc, sp.create_date, sp.modify_date, sl.principal_id;", "parameters": [], "description": "Lists application accounts with default/unchanged passwords and their privilege levels."}	null	low	f	t	00:01:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.789864
4740	sqlserver	instruct	Rotate passwords or decommission unused default accounts	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "For each default application account: (1) Check if the account has active sessions. (2) If no sessions in the last 90 days: disable the account: ALTER LOGIN [account] DISABLE; (3) If active sessions exist: rotate the password to a strong random password: ALTER LOGIN [account] WITH PASSWORD = 'new_strong_password'; (4) Coordinate with the application team for credential update. (5) Enable password policy: ALTER LOGIN [account] WITH CHECK_POLICY = ON; (6) Remove excessive privileges (sysadmin, db_owner) and grant only required permissions. (7) Document the account owner and purpose. (8) Schedule regular password rotation (90-day cycle)."}	null	medium	t	t	3 days	2026-02-24 13:10:27.789864
