4810	sqlserver	instruct	Standardize database ownership and fix orphaned owners	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "Rationalize ownership: (1) Fix orphaned owners (SID does not match any login): ALTER AUTHORIZATION ON DATABASE::[OrphanedDB] TO [sa]; (2) Standardize ownership to sa for all user databases (Microsoft best practice): ALTER AUTHORIZATION ON DATABASE::[UserDB] TO [sa]; (3) If sa is disabled, use a dedicated dbo-level account: CREATE LOGIN [db_owner_svc] WITH PASSWORD = '<strong_password>', CHECK_POLICY = ON; ALTER AUTHORIZATION ON DATABASE::[UserDB] TO [db_owner_svc]; (4) For Service Broker cross-database messaging, ownership standardization actually simplifies the trust model. (5) After standardizing ownership, chaining becomes less necessary because explicit permissions (not ownership-based bypass) should govern access. (6) Document the new ownership standard in the DBA runbook."}	null	medium	t	t	02:00:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.797143
