4895	sqlserver	instruct	Migrate xp_cmdshell calls to secure alternatives	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "For each identified usage, migrate to the appropriate alternative: (1) FILE_OPERATIONS (dir, copy, del, move): Use SQL Server SSIS File System Task, or PowerShell via SQL Agent CmdExec/PowerShell step type. (2) BCP_EXPORT: Use SSIS data flow tasks or BULK INSERT with FORMAT files. (3) NETWORK_OPERATIONS (ping, nslookup): Use CLR stored procedures with SAFE permission set, or move to application layer. (4) SQL_EXEC (osql, sqlcmd): Use linked servers, SQL Agent multi-step jobs, or SSIS Execute SQL Task. (5) For Agent jobs, change step type from T-SQL to CmdExec or PowerShell and remove the xp_cmdshell wrapper. Test each migration in non-production before deploying."}	null	low	f	t	5 days	2026-02-24 13:10:27.801005
