4970	sqlserver	instruct	Review assembly source code and downgrade permissions where possible	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "For each UNSAFE or EXTERNAL_ACCESS assembly: (1) Review the .NET source code to identify what elevated APIs are used. (2) If only mathematical/string processing: downgrade to SAFE using ALTER ASSEMBLY [Name] WITH PERMISSION_SET = SAFE. (3) If file I/O is needed: keep at EXTERNAL_ACCESS but sign with certificate. (4) If process execution or registry access: consider replacing with T-SQL or removing. (5) UNSAFE should only be used if P/Invoke or COM interop is absolutely required. (6) Test thoroughly after any permission change."}	null	medium	f	t	5 days	2026-02-24 13:10:27.801053
