5159	sqlserver	instruct	Set up key management and enable TDE	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "Option A (Built-in certificates, simpler): 1) Create a database master key in master. 2) Create a TDE certificate. 3) Back up the certificate and private key to a secure, separate location. 4) Create database encryption keys and enable TDE. 5) Establish a certificate backup and rotation schedule. Option B (EKM with Azure Key Vault, more secure): 1) Install the SQL Server Connector for Azure Key Vault. 2) Create a credential mapped to the Azure Key Vault. 3) Create an asymmetric key from Azure Key Vault. 4) Create DEKs using the asymmetric key. 5) Enable TDE. For both options: Document the key hierarchy and recovery procedures. Store backup passwords in a hardware security module or secure vault."}	{"sql": null, "description": "Disable TDE and remove encryption keys if key management proves unmanageable."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.851311
