5162	sqlserver	instruct	Enable TDE with design-aware approach	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "For databases WITHOUT FILESTREAM or In-Memory OLTP: Enable TDE normally. For databases WITH In-Memory OLTP (SQL 2016+): TDE is fully compatible. Enable TDE normally. For databases WITH FILESTREAM: 1) Enable TDE to protect data/log files. 2) FILESTREAM data in the file system will NOT be encrypted by TDE. 3) Implement EFS (Encrypting File System) or BitLocker for the FILESTREAM container. 4) Alternatively, migrate FILESTREAM data to VARBINARY(MAX) if feasible. 5) Document the gap: TDE + OS-level encryption for FILESTREAM data. Always: Back up the TDE certificate and private key to a secure, separate location."}	{"sql": null, "description": "Disable TDE if performance or compatibility issues arise."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.85205
