5177	sqlserver	instruct	Diagnose failure cause and re-enable TDE with safeguards	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "1) Review SQL Server error log for TDE-related errors from the previous attempt. 2) Common failure causes: expired certificate, insufficient disk space for encryption scan, performance degradation from hardware without AES-NI. 3) Address the root cause: renew expired certificates, ensure adequate disk space, verify AES-NI support. 4) Clean up orphaned DEKs: USE [db]; DROP DATABASE ENCRYPTION KEY; (only for databases in state 0 or 1). 5) Re-enable TDE during a maintenance window with monitoring. 6) Monitor encryption_state progression: 2 (in progress) -> 3 (complete). 7) Have a tested rollback plan ready."}	{"sql": null, "description": "ALTER DATABASE [db] SET ENCRYPTION OFF; to begin decryption if issues recur."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.856715
