5180	sqlserver	instruct	Establish key separation and enable TDE	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "For proper key separation: 1) Back up existing certificates and private keys immediately. 2) Store certificate backups in a physically separate secure location (different server, safe, HSM). 3) NEVER store certificate backups alongside database backups. Recommended approach: 1) Set up Azure Key Vault or on-premises HSM as EKM provider. 2) Create asymmetric keys in the external key store. 3) Use EKM-stored keys for TDE. 4) This ensures keys are never on the same disk as the database files. Minimum approach (no EKM): 1) Back up certificates to a separate network share or removable media. 2) Encrypt the backup password and store separately from the certificate file. 3) Test recovery by restoring certificates on a different server. 4) Document recovery procedures."}	{"sql": null, "description": "Disable TDE if key management proves unworkable."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.857371
