5217	sqlserver	instruct	Replace weak keys with AES-256 keys	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "1) For each weak key, create a new AES-256 replacement key. 2) Re-encrypt all data currently encrypted with the weak key using the new key. 3) The process: a) Open the old key. b) Open the new key. c) UPDATE table SET encrypted_col = EncryptByKey(Key_GUID('NewKey'), CONVERT(VARBINARY, DecryptByKey(encrypted_col))). d) Close both keys. 4) Update all application code and stored procedures to reference the new key. 5) After all data is re-encrypted and verified, drop the old key. 6) For TDE DEKs: ALTER DATABASE ENCRYPTION KEY REGENERATE WITH ALGORITHM = AES_256."}	{"sql": null, "description": "Keep the old key available for rollback. Re-encrypt data back to old key if needed."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.867181
