5249	sqlserver	instruct	Implement parameterization and QUOTENAME for all dynamic SQL	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "For each identified procedure: 1) For data values: use sp_executesql with parameter binding. 2) For table/column names: use QUOTENAME() and validate against a whitelist. Example: SET @sql = N'SELECT * FROM ' + QUOTENAME(@tableName) + N' WHERE id = @id'; EXEC sp_executesql @sql, N'@id INT', @id = @inputId; 3) Remove custom REPLACE-based escaping (it provides false security). 4) Validate identifiers against sys.tables or sys.columns before use. 5) Never trust input validation alone; always use parameterization as the primary defense."}	{"sql": null, "description": "Revert procedure changes if functionality breaks."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.874038
