5322	sqlserver	instruct	Create IP allowlist table and logon trigger	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "1) Create a table in master to hold approved IP addresses or CIDR prefixes: CREATE TABLE master.dbo.ip_allowlist (id INT IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY, ip_pattern VARCHAR(45) NOT NULL, description VARCHAR(255), added_date DATETIME DEFAULT GETDATE()). 2) Populate the allowlist with approved IP addresses from step 1. 3) Create a logon trigger: CREATE TRIGGER trg_ip_allowlist ON ALL SERVER FOR LOGON AS BEGIN DECLARE @ip VARCHAR(45) = EVENTDATA().value('(/EVENT_INSTANCE/ClientHost)[1]', 'VARCHAR(45)'); IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM master.dbo.ip_allowlist WHERE @ip LIKE ip_pattern) AND @ip <> '<local machine>' AND ORIGINAL_LOGIN() NOT IN ('sa') BEGIN ROLLBACK; END; END; 4) CRITICAL: Always exclude the sa account or DAC (Dedicated Admin Connection) to prevent lockout. 5) Test thoroughly: Connect from an approved IP first, then from a non-approved IP. 6) Add emergency bypass: DISABLE TRIGGER trg_ip_allowlist ON ALL SERVER (requires DAC if locked out)."}	{"sql": "DISABLE TRIGGER trg_ip_allowlist ON ALL SERVER;", "description": "Disable the logon trigger to restore unrestricted access."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.894311
