5350	sqlserver	instruct	Assign static non-default port and disable Browser	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "1) Select a non-standard static port (e.g., 14330). 2) In SQL Server Configuration Manager: a) Open TCP/IP Properties > IP Addresses > IP All. b) Set TCP Port to 14330. c) Clear TCP Dynamic Ports. 3) Disable SQL Server Browser: a) Stop the service: net stop SQLBrowser. b) Set startup to Disabled: sc config SQLBrowser start=disabled. 4) Update all connection strings with explicit port: Server=hostname,14330. 5) Update firewall: Block port 1433 TCP and 1434 UDP. Allow new port. 6) Restart SQL Server during maintenance window."}	{"sql": null, "description": "Re-enable Browser service and revert to original port."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.905534
