5365	sqlserver	instruct	Implement multi-layer scanning defenses	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "1) Change the listening port from 1433 to a non-standard port. 2) Disable SQL Server Browser service. 3) Block ports 1433 and 1434 (TCP and UDP) in the OS firewall. 4) Enable Force Encryption to prevent clear-text protocol detection. 5) Disable the sa login: ALTER LOGIN [sa] DISABLE. 6) Create an Extended Events session to capture failed login attempts: CREATE EVENT SESSION [FailedLogins] ON SERVER ADD EVENT sqlserver.error_reported(WHERE error_number = 18456) ADD TARGET package0.event_file(SET filename = N'FailedLogins.xel') WITH (STARTUP_STATE = ON). 7) Create a SQL Agent job to periodically check for high rates of failed logins and alert via Database Mail. 8) If possible, restrict the listener to bind only to private IP addresses."}	{"sql": null, "description": "Revert port and re-enable Browser if applications fail to connect."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.910129
