5368	sqlserver	instruct	Restrict outbound connections to approved endpoints only	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "1) For each identified outbound connection, determine if it is business-critical. 2) For Database Mail: Restrict SMTP relay to internal mail servers only. Document the approved SMTP server IPs. 3) For Linked Servers: a) Remove linked servers that are no longer needed. b) For required linked servers, document the destination IP/FQDN. c) Restrict linked server credentials (remove uses_self_credential). 4) For External Data Sources (PolyBase): Document approved external endpoints. 5) Configure outbound firewall rules on the SQL Server host: a) Block all outbound by default. b) Allow outbound only to specific approved destination IPs and ports. c) Allow DNS (port 53) to internal DNS servers only. 6) Disable CEIP/telemetry if not required: EXEC sp_configure 'customer feedback', 0; RECONFIGURE. 7) Document all approved outbound connections in the CMDB."}	{"sql": null, "description": "Re-open outbound firewall rules temporarily if critical features fail."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.911152
