5371	sqlserver	instruct	Harden or remove unnecessary linked servers	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "For each linked server: 1) Determine if it is still needed (check last access via sys.dm_exec_query_stats for linked server queries). 2) Remove unnecessary linked servers: EXEC sp_dropserver @server = N'server_name', @droplogins = 'droplogins'. 3) For required linked servers: a) Disable RPC out if not needed: EXEC sp_serveroption @server = N'server_name', @optname = 'rpc out', @optvalue = 'false'. b) Replace self-credential mapping with explicit low-privilege remote logins: EXEC sp_addlinkedsrvlogin @rmtsrvname = N'server_name', @useself = 'FALSE', @rmtuser = N'limited_user', @rmtpassword = N'strong_password'. c) Disable data access if only RPC is needed: EXEC sp_serveroption @server = N'server_name', @optname = 'data access', @optvalue = 'false'. 4) Restrict outbound firewall to allow connections only to the specific destination server IP and port. 5) Document each linked server's business justification."}	{"sql": null, "description": "Re-create linked servers with original settings from documentation."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.912288
