5373	sqlserver	verify	Inventory external data sources and external tables	{"sql": "SELECT\\n  (SELECT CAST(value_in_use AS INT) FROM sys.configurations\\n   WHERE name = 'polybase enabled') AS polybase_enabled,\\n  eds.name AS data_source_name,\\n  eds.type_desc AS source_type,\\n  eds.location AS remote_location,\\n  eds.credential_id,\\n  c.name AS credential_name\\nFROM sys.external_data_sources eds\\nLEFT JOIN sys.database_scoped_credentials c ON eds.credential_id = c.credential_id;\\n\\nSELECT et.name AS external_table_name,\\n  SCHEMA_NAME(et.schema_id) AS schema_name,\\n  eds.name AS data_source_name,\\n  eds.location AS remote_location\\nFROM sys.external_tables et\\nJOIN sys.external_data_sources eds ON et.data_source_id = eds.data_source_id;", "parameters": [], "description": "Lists all external data sources and tables that establish outbound connections."}	null	low	f	t	00:01:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.912805
5374	sqlserver	instruct	Remove unnecessary data sources and restrict outbound network	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "1) For each external data source, verify if it is actively used by querying sys.dm_exec_query_stats for external table references. 2) Remove unused external data sources: DROP EXTERNAL TABLE [table_name]; DROP EXTERNAL DATA SOURCE [source_name]; DROP DATABASE SCOPED CREDENTIAL [credential_name]. 3) For required external data sources: a) Document the exact endpoint URL/IP and port. b) Configure outbound firewall rules to allow connections ONLY to those specific endpoints. c) Use database scoped credentials with minimal permissions. d) Rotate credentials periodically. 4) If PolyBase is not needed: EXEC sp_configure 'polybase enabled', 0; RECONFIGURE. 5) If external scripts are not needed: EXEC sp_configure 'external scripts enabled', 0; RECONFIGURE. 6) Block all other outbound connections from the SQL Server host."}	{"sql": null, "description": "Re-create external data sources from documentation if they are needed."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.913329
