5387	sqlserver	instruct	Establish EOL tracking and alerting process	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "1) Create an inventory of all SQL Server instances with their version, edition, and lifecycle dates in the CMDB. 2) Subscribe to Microsoft Security Update notifications (https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide). 3) Create a SQL Agent job or monitoring check that runs monthly to report version and lifecycle status. 4) Define escalation thresholds: a) 12 months before end of mainstream support: Begin upgrade planning. b) 6 months before end of extended support: Upgrade project must be in progress. c) At end of support: Escalate to management as critical security risk. 5) Include version lifecycle review in quarterly security reviews. 6) For already-EOL versions: Begin immediate upgrade planning or implement compensating controls (network isolation, WAF, enhanced monitoring). 7) Track Microsoft lifecycle policy changes at https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/lifecycle/products."}	null	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.915871
5380	sqlserver	verify	Inventory cloud-facing linked servers and replication endpoints	{"sql": "SELECT s.name AS linked_server_name,\\n  s.data_source, s.provider, s.product,\\n  s.is_data_access_enabled, s.is_rpc_out_enabled\\nFROM sys.servers s\\nWHERE s.is_linked = 1\\n  AND (s.data_source LIKE '%.database.windows.net%'\\n    OR s.data_source LIKE '%.database.azure.com%'\\n    OR s.data_source LIKE '%.rds.amazonaws.com%'\\n    OR s.data_source LIKE '%.sql.azuresynapse.net%'\\n    OR s.data_source LIKE '%.googleapis.com%');\\n\\nSELECT ag.name AS ag_name, ar.replica_server_name,\\n  ar.endpoint_url, ar.availability_mode_desc\\nFROM sys.availability_groups ag\\nJOIN sys.availability_replicas ar ON ag.group_id = ar.group_id\\nWHERE ar.replica_server_name NOT LIKE '%' + CAST(SERVERPROPERTY('MachineName') AS NVARCHAR(128)) + '%';\\n\\nSELECT ds.name, ds.type_desc, ds.location\\nFROM sys.external_data_sources ds\\nWHERE ds.location LIKE 'https://%'\\n  OR ds.location LIKE 'wasbs://%'\\n  OR ds.location LIKE 'abfss://%'\\n  OR ds.location LIKE 's3://%';", "parameters": [], "description": "Identifies all outbound connections to cloud services."}	null	low	f	t	00:01:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.916187
