5381	sqlserver	instruct	Migrate cloud connections to private endpoints or VPN	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "For Azure SQL targets: 1) Create an Azure Private Endpoint for the target Azure SQL instance. 2) Configure private DNS resolution to route the FQDN to the private IP. 3) Update linked server data_source to use the private endpoint FQDN. 4) Enable Force Encryption on the linked server connection. For AWS RDS targets: 1) Set up VPN (Site-to-Site) or AWS Direct Connect between on-premises and the AWS VPC. 2) Ensure the RDS instance is in a private subnet. 3) Update linked server data_source to use the private DNS name. For AG replicas across networks: 1) Use a VPN tunnel between sites. 2) Ensure the AG endpoint uses certificate authentication. 3) Verify encryption is configured on the database mirroring endpoint. For all connections: a) Configure outbound firewall to allow ONLY the specific private endpoint IPs. b) Block all other outbound traffic on SQL Server ports. c) Enable TLS 1.2 minimum on all connections."}	{"sql": null, "description": "Revert to rootcause endpoint connectivity temporarily while troubleshooting private connectivity."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.916543
