5408	sqlserver	instruct	Plan and execute staged patch deployment	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "1) Build a dependency map: SQL Server CU -> client drivers -> CLR assemblies -> linked server providers. 2) For each dependency: a) Check vendor compatibility matrix for the target CU. b) Identify if the dependency needs updating before or after the SQL patch. 3) Staged deployment plan: a) Stage 1: Update client drivers on application servers (no SQL restart needed). b) Stage 2: Update OLEDB/ODBC providers for linked servers. c) Stage 3: Apply SQL Server CU during maintenance window. d) Stage 4: Recompile CLR assemblies if needed against the new SQL version. 4) For CLR assemblies: a) Test compilation against the new SQL version in staging. b) If UNSAFE assemblies fail: Check if 'clr strict security' (SQL 2017+) is blocking them. c) Sign assemblies with a certificate and create a login from that certificate. 5) For linked server providers: a) Verify the provider DLL version is compatible with the new CU. b) Update Microsoft OLE DB Driver if the linked server uses SQLNCLI (deprecated). 6) Keep compatibility level unchanged during patching to minimize variables."}	{"sql": null, "description": "Uninstall the CU and revert to the previous build if critical issues are found."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.92249
