5413	sqlserver	verify	Check current build branch and patch staleness	{"sql": "SELECT\\n  SERVERPROPERTY('ProductVersion') AS product_version,\\n  SERVERPROPERTY('ProductLevel') AS product_level,\\n  SERVERPROPERTY('ProductUpdateLevel') AS product_update_level,\\n  SERVERPROPERTY('ProductBuildType') AS product_build_type,\\n  CASE\\n    WHEN SERVERPROPERTY('ProductBuildType') = 'GDR' THEN 'Security-only branch (minimal patches)'\\n    WHEN SERVERPROPERTY('ProductBuildType') = 'OD' THEN 'Cumulative Update branch (full patches)'\\n    ELSE 'Unknown branch'\\n  END AS branch_description;\\n\\nSELECT sqlserver_start_time,\\n  DATEDIFF(DAY, sqlserver_start_time, GETDATE()) AS days_since_restart\\nFROM sys.dm_os_sys_info;", "parameters": [], "description": "Identifies the current update branch and how current the patch level is."}	null	low	f	t	00:01:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.923388
5414	sqlserver	instruct	Establish risk-based patch prioritization	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "1) Choose the appropriate update branch: a) GDR (Security-only): For production systems where stability is paramount. Smaller updates, security fixes only, lower regression risk. b) CU (Cumulative): For systems that need all fixes including performance and functionality. Larger updates, higher regression risk but more comprehensive. 2) Create a patch prioritization matrix: a) CRITICAL (Apply within 14 days): Remote Code Execution (RCE) vulnerabilities, authentication bypass, SQL injection in engine. b) HIGH (Apply within 30 days): Privilege escalation, information disclosure of credentials. c) MEDIUM (Apply within 90 days): Denial of service, information disclosure of metadata. d) LOW (Apply with next scheduled CU): Non-security cumulative improvements. 3) Automation: a) Create a monitoring job that checks the current build against Microsoft's latest release. b) Alert when more than 30 days behind on the GDR branch. c) Subscribe to SQL Server release blog (https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/sql-server-blog/bg-p/SQLServer). 4) For each patch cycle: a) Review the CVE list in the release notes. b) Assess exploitability (are there known exploits?). c) Apply based on the priority matrix, not on a fixed schedule."}	null	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.923731
