5432	sqlserver	instruct	Deploy DDM for display protection and Always Encrypted for true encryption	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "Layer 1 - Dynamic Data Masking (immediate, zero performance overhead): 1) Apply DDM to PII columns: a) SSN: ALTER TABLE [users] ALTER COLUMN [ssn] ADD MASKED WITH (FUNCTION = 'partial(0,\\"XXX-XX-\\",4)'). b) Email: ALTER TABLE [users] ALTER COLUMN [email] ADD MASKED WITH (FUNCTION = 'email()'). c) Phone: ALTER TABLE [users] ALTER COLUMN [phone] ADD MASKED WITH (FUNCTION = 'partial(0,\\"XXX-XXX-\\",4)'). d) Credit card: ALTER TABLE [users] ALTER COLUMN [credit_card] ADD MASKED WITH (FUNCTION = 'partial(0,\\"XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-\\",4)'). 2) Revoke UNMASK from all non-essential users: REVOKE UNMASK FROM [user_name]. 3) Grant UNMASK only to specific principals that need unmasked data. Layer 2 - Always Encrypted (for highest-sensitivity columns): 4) Apply Always Encrypted to SSN, credit card, bank account columns. 5) DDM and Always Encrypted can coexist on different columns. Layer 3 - Remove custom masking: 6) Drop custom masking UDFs, views, and stored procedures. 7) Update applications to query the base table directly (DDM handles masking transparently)."}	{"sql": null, "description": "Remove DDM: ALTER TABLE [table] ALTER COLUMN [column] DROP MASKED. Re-create custom masking objects if needed."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.927618
