5441	sqlserver	instruct	Deploy DDM immediately and plan Always Encrypted for high-sensitivity columns	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "Quick Win - Dynamic Data Masking (deploy immediately, zero performance impact): 1) Identify all PII-candidate columns (SSN, email, phone, credit card, DOB). 2) Apply masking functions: a) ALTER TABLE [users] ALTER COLUMN [ssn] ADD MASKED WITH (FUNCTION = 'partial(0, \\"XXX-XX-\\", 4)'). b) ALTER TABLE [users] ALTER COLUMN [email] ADD MASKED WITH (FUNCTION = 'email()'). c) ALTER TABLE [users] ALTER COLUMN [phone] ADD MASKED WITH (FUNCTION = 'default()'). d) ALTER TABLE [users] ALTER COLUMN [credit_card] ADD MASKED WITH (FUNCTION = 'partial(0, \\"XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-\\", 4)'). 3) Revoke UNMASK from all users except those who need it: REVOKE UNMASK FROM [rootcause]; GRANT UNMASK TO [specific_admin_role]. 4) DDM limitations: a) sysadmin and db_owner always see unmasked data. b) SELECT INTO copies unmasked data. c) DDM is display-level only, not true encryption. Long-term - Always Encrypted (plan and deploy): 5) For SSN, credit card, bank account: Deploy Always Encrypted (see RC01/RC02 resolutions). 6) DDM and Always Encrypted serve different purposes and complement each other."}	{"sql": null, "description": "Remove DDM: ALTER TABLE [table] ALTER COLUMN [column] DROP MASKED."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.930433
