5447	sqlserver	instruct	Narrow audit scope and configure PII-safe logging	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "1) Replace statement-level DML auditing with group-level auditing: a) Remove individual SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE actions. b) Use SCHEMA_OBJECT_ACCESS_GROUP instead (captures object access without full SQL text). c) ALTER SERVER AUDIT SPECIFICATION [spec_name] DROP (SELECT ON OBJECT::schema.table BY [rootcause]). d) ALTER SERVER AUDIT SPECIFICATION [spec_name] ADD (SCHEMA_OBJECT_ACCESS_GROUP). 2) For Extended Events: a) Remove sql_batch_completed and sql_statement_completed events from sessions not needed for active debugging. b) If statement capture is needed, add a predicate filter to exclude PII tables: ADD EVENT sqlserver.sql_statement_completed (WHERE sqlserver.database_name <> 'PII_Database'). c) Set max_dispatch_latency to limit XE file accumulation. 3) For compliance requirements that mandate statement capture: a) Enable parameterized query enforcement (FORCED parameterization) so literals are replaced with placeholders in logs. b) ALTER DATABASE [db_name] SET PARAMETERIZATION FORCED. 4) Restrict access to audit files: a) Move audit files to a restricted directory. b) Grant read access only to security team members."}	{"sql": null, "description": "Revert audit specifications to previous configuration."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.932445
