5450	sqlserver	execute	Enable forced parameterization and optimize for ad hoc workloads	{"sql": "-- Enable optimize for ad hoc workloads to reduce single-use plan cache\\nEXEC sp_configure 'optimize for ad hoc workloads', 1;\\nRECONFIGURE;", "parameters": [], "description": "Enables optimization that reduces plan cache pollution from ad-hoc queries."}	{"sql": "EXEC sp_configure 'optimize for ad hoc workloads', 0; RECONFIGURE;", "description": "Revert ad hoc optimization."}	low	t	t	00:01:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.932761
5451	sqlserver	instruct	Enable forced parameterization on databases with PII	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "1) For each database containing PII columns: ALTER DATABASE [db_name] SET PARAMETERIZATION FORCED. 2) Monitor for query plan regressions: a) Enable Query Store before changing parameterization. b) Compare query performance before and after. c) If specific queries regress, use plan guides to override forced parameterization for those queries: sp_create_plan_guide @name = 'guide_name', @stmt = N'SELECT ...', @type = N'SQL', @hints = N'OPTION (PARAMETERIZATION SIMPLE)'. 3) Communicate to development teams: a) All new queries should use parameterized queries (sp_executesql, SqlCommand.Parameters). b) String concatenation for SQL is a security defect, not just a performance issue. c) Add static analysis rules to detect string concatenation in SQL queries. 4) FORCED parameterization effects: a) Most literal values in WHERE clauses are replaced with parameters. b) Plan cache stores parameterized plans, not literal values. c) Logs and audit trails capture the parameterized form, not PII literals."}	{"sql": "ALTER DATABASE [db_name] SET PARAMETERIZATION SIMPLE;", "description": "Revert to simple parameterization."}	medium	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.933226
