5460	sqlserver	instruct	Filter XE sessions and secure Query Store data	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "1) For Extended Events sessions: a) Add predicate filters to exclude encryption function calls: WHERE sqlserver.sql_text NOT LIKE '%EncryptBy%' AND sqlserver.sql_text NOT LIKE '%DecryptBy%'. b) If the session is for debugging only, stop it: ALTER EVENT SESSION [session_name] ON SERVER STATE = STOP. c) Remove startup_state = ON from debugging sessions. 2) For Query Store: a) Query Store captures query text which may contain sensitive function parameters. b) The risk is mitigated if applications use parameterized queries (parameters are not stored in query text). c) Restrict access to Query Store data: DENY SELECT ON sys.query_store_query_text TO [non_admin_role]. d) Set appropriate cleanup policies: ALTER DATABASE [db] SET QUERY_STORE (CLEANUP_POLICY = (STALE_QUERY_THRESHOLD_DAYS = 30)). 3) Enable FORCED PARAMETERIZATION on databases using encryption functions: a) This ensures literal values are replaced with parameters before reaching the plan cache and Query Store. 4) Restrict access to XE target files: a) Move .xel files to a restricted directory. b) Set MAX_FILE_SIZE and MAX_ROLLOVER_FILES to limit accumulation."}	null	low	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.935263
