5465	sqlserver	verify	Identify XE sessions with low or zero duration thresholds	{"sql": "SELECT ses.name AS session_name,\\n  sese.event_name,\\n  ses.startup_state AS starts_with_server\\nFROM sys.dm_xe_sessions ses\\nJOIN sys.dm_xe_session_events sese ON ses.address = sese.event_session_address\\nWHERE sese.event_name IN ('sql_batch_completed', 'sql_statement_completed',\\n  'rpc_completed', 'query_post_execution_showplan')\\nORDER BY ses.name, sese.event_name;\\n\\nSELECT ses.name AS session_name, sese.event_name,\\n  CASE WHEN sese.event_name LIKE '%showplan%'\\n    THEN 'CAPTURES FULL XML PLAN WITH LITERALS'\\n    ELSE 'CAPTURES QUERY TEXT'\\n  END AS exposure_level\\nFROM sys.dm_xe_sessions ses\\nJOIN sys.dm_xe_session_events sese ON ses.address = sese.event_session_address\\nWHERE sese.event_name IN ('query_post_execution_showplan',\\n  'query_post_compilation_showplan');", "parameters": [], "description": "Lists XE sessions capturing query text and showplans that may contain PII literals."}	null	low	f	t	00:01:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.936426
5466	sqlserver	instruct	Raise duration thresholds or stop unnecessary sessions	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "1) For each identified XE session: a) If the session is for active debugging only: Stop it and disable startup_state: ALTER EVENT SESSION [session_name] ON SERVER STATE = STOP. b) If the session is for ongoing performance monitoring: Raise the duration threshold to capture only genuinely slow queries. 2) Recommended thresholds: a) For sql_batch_completed/sql_statement_completed: Set duration > 5000000 microseconds (5 seconds). b) This captures only slow queries, excluding the fast INSERT/UPDATE statements that typically contain PII. c) ALTER EVENT SESSION [session_name] ON SERVER DROP EVENT sqlserver.sql_batch_completed; ALTER EVENT SESSION [session_name] ON SERVER ADD EVENT sqlserver.sql_batch_completed (WHERE duration > 5000000). 3) Remove showplan events from production sessions: a) query_post_execution_showplan captures full XML plans WITH literal values. b) This is the highest PII exposure risk from XE. c) Use Query Store for plan analysis instead (it does not capture literal values in plans). 4) Restrict XE file access: a) Move .xel files to a restricted directory. b) Set MAX_FILE_SIZE and MAX_ROLLOVER_FILES to limit data accumulation. 5) Create an XE cleanup job: Delete .xel files older than 7 days."}	{"sql": null, "description": "Re-add events with the original thresholds if performance monitoring is insufficient."}	low	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.936891
