5470	sqlserver	instruct	Replace stale traces with filtered XE sessions if needed	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "If ongoing performance monitoring is needed: 1) Create an XE session with appropriate duration filters: CREATE EVENT SESSION [PerfMonitor] ON SERVER ADD EVENT sqlserver.sql_batch_completed (WHERE duration > 5000000) ADD TARGET package0.event_file (SET filename = N'PerfMonitor.xel', max_file_size = 100, max_rollover_files = 5) WITH (MAX_DISPATCH_LATENCY = 30 SECONDS, STARTUP_STATE = ON). 2) XE advantages over SQL Trace: a) Lower performance overhead. b) Fine-grained predicate filtering. c) Better file management with max_rollover_files. d) Can exclude specific databases or query patterns. 3) Clean up old trace files: a) Locate and securely delete .trc files from the old traces. b) Use EXEC sys.fn_trace_getinfo(0) to find trace file paths. 4) SQL Trace is deprecated in SQL Server 2012+ and will be removed in a future version."}	null	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.93763
