5473	sqlserver	instruct	Configure log rotation and restrict file permissions	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "1) Configure error log rotation: a) Set a reasonable number of error log files (6-12): EXEC sp_configure 'number of errorlog files', 12; RECONFIGURE. b) Create a SQL Agent job to cycle the error log weekly: EXEC sp_cycle_errorlog. c) This limits the time window of PII accumulation. 2) Set error log maximum size (SQL 2012+): a) Use the registry or SQL Server Configuration Manager. b) Default is unlimited. Set to 20-50 MB to force rotation. 3) Restrict file permissions on log directories: a) Navigate to the SQL Server LOG directory. b) Remove the Everyone group and Users group. c) Grant Full Control to: SQL Server service account, SQL Server Agent service account, Local Administrators (DBA team). d) Remove all other permissions. 4) Apply the same permissions to: a) Default trace file directory. b) Extended Events .xel file directory. c) Backup directories. d) Data and log file directories. 5) Encrypt the log volume: a) Enable BitLocker on the volume containing LOG files. b) Or use EFS (Encrypting File System) on the LOG directory. c) This protects log files at rest. 6) Automate log cleanup: a) Create a SQL Agent job to delete .xel, .trc, and .mdmp files older than 30 days."}	null	low	t	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.938263
