927	sqlserver	instruct	Address root network or I/O bottleneck at intermediate node	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "After stopping lag amplification, resolve the underlying bottleneck at the intermediate node. Check: (1) Network bandwidth between primary and intermediate using Windows Performance Monitor (Network Interface\\\\Bytes Total/sec). (2) Disk I/O on the intermediate node — if redo_queue_size is high, the disk subsystem may be the bottleneck (check sys.dm_io_virtual_file_stats). (3) CPU saturation from decompression — review log decompression counters. (4) If the intermediate node is a distributed AG global primary, check if it is also running a heavy workload that competes with the forwarder role. Address the specific bottleneck found, then restore synchronous commit mode once queues drain."}	null	low	f	t	\N	2026-02-24 13:10:27.201358
953	sqlserver	instruct	Free disk space via log backup and old file cleanup	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["database_name: database with log on the full volume", "other_volume: network share or separate local volume with available space"], "description": "Perform immediate space recovery actions in order of safety:\\n\\n1. Back up transaction logs to a different volume to enable truncation:\\n   BACKUP LOG <database_name> TO DISK = N'<other_volume>\\\\<db>_log.bak'\\n\\n2. After backup, shrink VLF space only if log is bloated (not routine):\\n   USE <database_name>; DBCC SHRINKFILE (<log_file_name>, TRUNCATEONLY);\\n\\n3. Delete old backup files, trace files, and error logs from the volume:\\n   xp_cmdshell 'del /Q C:\\\\backup\\\\*.bak' -- adjust path as appropriate\\n   EXEC sp_cycle_errorlog; -- rotates current error log to free space\\n\\n4. Compress existing backups if space allows:\\n   EXEC sp_configure 'backup compression default', 1; RECONFIGURE;\\n\\n5. Move tempdb files to a larger volume (requires restart):\\n   ALTER DATABASE tempdb MODIFY FILE (NAME = tempdev, FILENAME = 'D:\\\\tempdb\\\\tempdb.mdf');\\n   ALTER DATABASE tempdb MODIFY FILE (NAME = templog, FILENAME = 'D:\\\\tempdb\\\\templog.ldf');"}	null	medium	t	f	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.204674
966	sqlserver	instruct	Distribute new rootcause certificates to partner replicas	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["PartnerName: server name of each partner replica"], "description": "For certificate-based authentication, each replica must trust the other replicas' certificates. After creating the new certificate on each replica:\\n\\n1. Copy each replica's exported .cer file to all other replicas\\n\\n2. On each replica, import the other replicas' new certificates:\\n   USE master;\\n   CREATE LOGIN [AG_Login_<PartnerName>] FROM WINDOWS; -- if using login-based\\n   -- OR for certificate auth:\\n   CREATE USER [AG_User_<PartnerName>] WITHOUT LOGIN;\\n   CREATE CERTIFICATE [AG_Cert_<PartnerName>]\\n     AUTHORIZATION [AG_User_<PartnerName>]\\n     FROM FILE = N'C:\\\\Temp\\\\AG_Endpoint_Cert_New_<PartnerName>.cer';\\n   GRANT CONNECT ON ENDPOINT::[Hadr_endpoint] TO [AG_User_<PartnerName>];\\n\\n3. After updating all replicas, verify connectivity:\\n   SELECT ar.replica_server_name, drs.connected_state_desc\\n   FROM sys.dm_hadr_database_replica_states drs\\n   JOIN sys.availability_replicas ar ON drs.replica_id = ar.replica_id;"}	null	medium	t	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.204683
971	sqlserver	instruct	Apply Microsoft-recommended AV exclusions on all cluster nodes	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "Configure the following exclusions in the anti-virus product on EVERY cluster node (Microsoft KB 309422):\\n\\nFILE EXTENSION EXCLUSIONS:\\n  .mdf, .ndf, .ldf  -- SQL Server data and log files\\n  .bak, .trn        -- Backup files\\n  .trc              -- Trace files\\n  .sql              -- SQL scripts\\n  .dat              -- Replication files\\n\\nDIRECTORY EXCLUSIONS (adjust paths to match installation):\\n  C:\\\\Program Files\\\\Microsoft SQL Server\\\\\\n  SQL Server data file directories (all volumes with .mdf/.ldf files)\\n  SQL Server backup directories\\n  WSFC quorum disk path\\n  C:\\\\Windows\\\\Cluster\\\\\\n\\nPROCESS EXCLUSIONS:\\n  sqlservr.exe  -- SQL Server database engine\\n  sqlagent.exe  -- SQL Server Agent\\n  sqlwriter.exe -- SQL Writer service\\n  clussvc.exe   -- Windows Cluster service\\n  msdtc.exe     -- Distributed Transaction Coordinator\\n\\nNote: The exact exclusion configuration interface varies by AV product. Consult your security team and vendor documentation. A temporary test exclusion (revert after validation) can confirm AV is the cause."}	null	medium	t	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.204686
1142	sqlserver	configure	Migrate to local file share witness if cloud connectivity is unreliable	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["witness_server", "share_name"], "description": "If cloud connectivity cannot be reliably maintained, migrate to a local file share witness: (1) Identify a suitable witness server: must NOT be a cluster node; should be in a different fault domain from the cluster nodes; can be a domain controller, management server, or dedicated utility server. (2) Create the witness share on that server (see RC03 steps for share creation details). (3) Reconfigure quorum: Set-ClusterQuorum -FileShareWitness '\\\\\\\\<witness_server>\\\\<share_name>'. (4) Verify: Get-ClusterQuorum. (5) Confirm witness is UP: (Get-ClusterNode '<witness_server>').State."}	{"sql": null, "description": "To revert back to cloud witness: Set-ClusterQuorum -CloudWitness -AccountName '<storage_account>' -AccessKey '<key>'."}	medium	t	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236529
997	sqlserver	instruct	Restore file share witness access or fix cloud witness connectivity	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "For FILE_SHARE_WITNESS that is OFFLINE:\\n1. Verify the file server hosting the witness share is running\\n2. Check share path accessibility from all cluster nodes: Test-Path '\\\\\\\\FileServer\\\\WitnessShare'\\n3. Verify cluster computer accounts (CLUSTERNAME$) have FULL CONTROL on the share\\n4. Check firewall rules between cluster nodes and the file server (TCP 445)\\n5. If the file server has moved, update the witness path in Failover Cluster Manager:\\n   Cluster -> Properties -> Quorum -> Configure Cluster Quorum -> File Share Witness -> enter new UNC path\\n\\nFor CLOUD_WITNESS that is OFFLINE:\\n1. Verify Azure storage account exists and is accessible\\n2. Check that 'Allow Azure services' firewall rule is enabled on the storage account\\n3. Verify cluster nodes have network access to *.blob.core.windows.net on port 443\\n4. Regenerate storage account access key if authentication changed:\\n   Failover Cluster Manager -> Cluster -> Configure Cluster Quorum -> Cloud Witness -> enter storage account name and new key"}	null	low	f	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.204704
998	sqlserver	instruct	Reconfigure cluster to use alternative witness if original cannot be restored	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["NewServer: UNC-accessible file server for new file share witness", "WitnessShare: share name for the new witness", "StorageAccountName: Azure storage account name for cloud witness", "AccessKey: Azure storage account access key"], "description": "If the original witness cannot be restored, reconfigure the cluster to use an alternative:\\n\\nOption A — New File Share Witness:\\n  Set-ClusterQuorum -FileShareWitness '\\\\\\\\NewServer\\\\WitnessShare'\\n  Requirements: Share on a server NOT in the cluster, accessible from all nodes\\n\\nOption B — Cloud Witness (recommended for new deployments):\\n  Set-ClusterQuorum -CloudWitness -AccountName '<StorageAccountName>' -AccessKey '<Key1>'\\n  Requirements: Azure storage account in a different region/datacenter from cluster nodes\\n\\nOption C — No witness (only for clusters with odd node count):\\n  Set-ClusterQuorum -NodeMajority\\n  WARNING: Only use for 3+ node clusters; 2-node clusters lose failover resilience without a witness\\n\\nAfter reconfiguring, verify the new witness appears ONLINE in:\\n  Get-ClusterQuorum"}	null	medium	t	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.204704
1022	sqlserver	instruct	Fix endpoint authentication — grant CONNECT to service accounts	{"sql": null, "parameters": [{"name": "Hadr_endpoint", "description": "Endpoint name"}, {"name": "DOMAIN\\\\SQLServiceAccount", "description": "Service account of the remote replica's SQL Server"}], "description": "If endpoints use Windows authentication, grant CONNECT permission to the SQL Server service accounts of all other replicas: GRANT CONNECT ON ENDPOINT::[Hadr_endpoint] TO [DOMAIN\\\\SQLServiceAccount]; If certificate-based auth is used, verify certificate validity (not expired), exchange certificates between instances, and ensure the certificate login has CONNECT permission on the endpoint. Check SQL error log for 'login failed' or 'connection_handshake' errors to identify the specific auth failure."}	null	medium	t	f	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.204718
1165	sqlserver	instruct	Prepare the new witness resource	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "For a File Share Witness: (1) Create the share directory on the target server. (2) Share it with 'New-SmbShare -Name \\"<share_name>\\" -Path \\"<path>\\" -FullAccess \\"<DOMAIN>\\\\<ClusterComputerObject$>\\"'. (3) Grant the cluster computer account (DOMAIN\\\\CLUSTERNAME$) Full Control on both the share and NTFS permissions. For a Cloud Witness: (1) Create or identify an Azure Storage Account in a region separate from all cluster sites. (2) Copy the storage account name and either of the two access keys from the Azure Portal."}	null	low	t	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.226581
1128	sqlserver	configure	Reconfigure quorum model for new node count	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["storage_account", "access_key", "witness_share_path"], "description": "Adjust the quorum model to match the new cluster topology: (1) Open Failover Cluster Manager > right-click cluster > More Actions > Configure Cluster Quorum Settings. (2) For 3-4 nodes: use 'Node Majority' (no witness needed; tolerates floor(N/2) failures). (3) For 2 nodes or even node counts: use 'Node and File Share Majority' with a file share witness on a third server, or 'Cloud Witness' using Azure Blob Storage. (4) Via PowerShell to set cloud witness: Set-ClusterQuorum -CloudWitness -AccountName '<storage_account>' -AccessKey '<key>'. (5) Via PowerShell to set file share witness: Set-ClusterQuorum -FileShareWitness '\\\\\\\\<server>\\\\<share>'. (6) Verify: Get-ClusterQuorum."}	{"sql": null, "description": "To revert quorum model: Set-ClusterQuorum -NodeMajority (for odd node counts) or reconfigure the previous witness type via Failover Cluster Manager."}	medium	t	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.231814
1137	sqlserver	verify	Confirm file share witness state and access path	{"sql": "SELECT\\n  cm.member_name AS witness_server,\\n  cm.member_type_desc,\\n  cm.member_state_desc,\\n  c.quorum_type_desc\\nFROM sys.dm_hadr_cluster c\\nCROSS JOIN sys.dm_hadr_cluster_members cm\\nWHERE c.quorum_type_desc LIKE '%FILE%'\\n  OR cm.member_type_desc LIKE '%FILE%'\\nORDER BY cm.member_type_desc;", "parameters": ["witness_server", "share_name"], "description": "Confirm the witness type is FILE_SHARE_MAJORITY and record the witness server name. Then from a cluster node in PowerShell: (1) Get the share path: Get-ClusterQuorum | Select-Object QuorumResource, QuorumType. (2) Test share access: Test-Path '\\\\\\\\<witness_server>\\\\<share_name>'. (3) Test SMB port: Test-NetConnection -ComputerName '<witness_server>' -Port 445. Document whether the failure is SMB service down, share missing, or permission denied."}	null	low	f	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236524
1138	sqlserver	configure	Restore SMB service and file share on witness server	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["share_name", "DOMAIN", "ClusterName", "witness_server"], "description": "On the witness server: (1) Check if Server service (SMB) is running: Get-Service LanmanServer. If stopped: Start-Service LanmanServer; Set-Service LanmanServer -StartupType Automatic. (2) Verify the share exists: Get-SmbShare -Name '<share_name>'. If missing, recreate it: New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path 'C:\\\\ClusterWitness' -Force; New-SmbShare -Name '<share_name>' -Path 'C:\\\\ClusterWitness' -FullAccess '<DOMAIN>\\\\<ClusterName>$'. (3) Verify NTFS permissions: The cluster computer account (<DOMAIN>\\\\<ClusterName>$) needs Full Control on both the share and the folder. icacls 'C:\\\\ClusterWitness' /grant '<DOMAIN>\\\\<ClusterName>$:(OI)(CI)F' /T. (4) Verify the path is accessible from all cluster nodes: Test-Path '\\\\\\\\<witness_server>\\\\<share_name>' run from each node."}	{"sql": null, "description": "To remove a recreated share: Remove-SmbShare -Name '<share_name>' -Force. This does not affect cluster quorum configuration; the cluster will show the witness as DOWN until a new witness is configured."}	low	f	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236525
5642	postgresql	configure	Tune replication settings to reduce standby lag	{"sql": "ALTER SYSTEM SET max_wal_senders = ':max_senders';\\nALTER SYSTEM SET wal_keep_size = ':wal_keep_size';\\nSELECT pg_reload_conf();", "parameters": ["max_senders", "wal_keep_size"], "description": "Increases WAL sender capacity and WAL retention to ensure standby can keep up"}	{"sql": "ALTER SYSTEM RESET max_wal_senders;\\nALTER SYSTEM RESET wal_keep_size;\\nSELECT pg_reload_conf();", "description": "Reset replication settings to defaults"}	medium	t	t	1-5 minutes	2026-02-25 08:59:43.77256
1150	sqlserver	configure	Migrate to file share or cloud witness if disk cannot be recovered	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["witness_server", "share_name", "azure_storage_account", "key", "old_disk_resource_name"], "description": "If the disk witness cannot be recovered, migrate to a more resilient witness type: (1) For file share witness: Create a share on a server outside the cluster (see RC03 for creation steps), then: Set-ClusterQuorum -FileShareWitness '\\\\\\\\<witness_server>\\\\<share_name>'. (2) For cloud witness (recommended for Azure-connected environments): Set-ClusterQuorum -CloudWitness -AccountName '<azure_storage_account>' -AccessKey '<key>'. (3) Verify the new witness is UP: Get-ClusterQuorum; Get-ClusterNode. (4) Remove the failed disk witness resource from the cluster after migration: Remove-ClusterResource -Name '<old_disk_resource_name>' -Force (only after confirming new witness is UP)."}	{"sql": null, "description": "To revert to disk witness: Reconfigure quorum in Failover Cluster Manager to use the original disk (if recovered): Set-ClusterQuorum -DiskWitness '<disk_resource_name>'."}	medium	t	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236534
1168	sqlserver	instruct	Diagnose TLS connectivity to cloud witness endpoint	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "From each cluster node, test connectivity to the cloud witness storage account: (1) 'Test-NetConnection -ComputerName \\"<storage_account>.blob.core.windows.net\\" -Port 443' — should show TcpTestSucceeded: True. (2) In PowerShell: '[Net.ServicePointManager]::SecurityProtocol' — should include 'Tls12'. (3) Check the cluster log for TLS errors: 'Get-ClusterLog -Destination C:\\\\Temp\\\\ClusterLog' then search for 'SSL', 'TLS', or 'certificate' in the log. (4) Check Windows Event Log: System log for Schannel event IDs 36871 (fatal alert), 36874 (TLS connection), 36888 (connection attempt failure)."}	null	low	f	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236544
