1169	sqlserver	instruct	Enable TLS 1.2 and update cipher suites on cluster nodes	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "If TLS 1.2 is not enabled or cipher suites are mismatched: (1) Enable TLS 1.2 via registry (or use IISCrypto tool on each node): Set HKLM\\\\SYSTEM\\\\CurrentControlSet\\\\Control\\\\SecurityProviders\\\\SCHANNEL\\\\Protocols\\\\TLS 1.2\\\\Client\\\\Enabled = 1 and DisabledByDefault = 0. (2) Ensure the cipher suite TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 or TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 is present and not disabled: 'Get-TlsCipherSuite | Select-Object Name'. (3) Install any missing Windows root certificate updates: run 'certutil -generateSSTFromWU roots.sst' and import. (4) If a proxy performs TLS inspection, configure it to bypass *.blob.core.windows.net or add the proxy's root CA to the Windows certificate store."}	null	medium	t	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236545
514	sqlserver	execute	Grant appropriate roles to individual DBA logins	{"sql": "-- For genuine DBAs who need sysadmin\\nALTER SERVER ROLE sysadmin ADD MEMBER [<DOMAIN\\\\individual_dba>];\\n\\n-- For users who need lesser access\\nALTER SERVER ROLE serveradmin ADD MEMBER [<DOMAIN\\\\server_ops>];\\nALTER SERVER ROLE dbcreator ADD MEMBER [<DOMAIN\\\\dev_lead>];", "parameters": ["DOMAIN\\\\individual_dba", "DOMAIN\\\\server_ops", "DOMAIN\\\\dev_lead"], "description": "Grants the appropriate server role to individual accounts rather than relying on a broad AD group."}	{"sql": "ALTER SERVER ROLE sysadmin DROP MEMBER [<DOMAIN\\\\individual_dba>];", "description": "Remove incorrectly added individual logins."}	medium	t	t	00:15:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.148386
1173	sqlserver	instruct	Update witness configuration to reflect current infrastructure	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "From an elevated PowerShell prompt, apply the correction matching the stale element identified in step 1: (A) For a renamed or moved file share witness: 'Set-ClusterQuorum -FileShareWitness \\\\\\\\<new_server>\\\\<new_share>'. Verify the cluster computer account has Full Control on the new share. (B) For a cloud witness with rotated storage key: 'Set-ClusterQuorum -CloudWitness -AccountName \\"<account>\\" -AccessKey \\"<new_key>\\"'. (C) For a witness server with a changed IP — update DNS as per DNS resolution fix, then verify WSFC resolves the new address; if using an IP-based share path, update the path: 'Set-ClusterQuorum -FileShareWitness \\\\\\\\<new_ip>\\\\<share>'. After any change, run 'Get-ClusterQuorum' to confirm the updated path."}	null	medium	t	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236547
1177	sqlserver	instruct	Bring witness server back online and verify service availability	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "After maintenance is complete on the witness server: (1) Start the Server service if it was stopped: 'Start-Service -Name LanmanServer'. (2) Verify the file share is accessible: 'Test-Path \\\\\\\\<witness_server>\\\\<share_name>'. (3) For a cloud witness, no action is needed — the cloud service is always available, and WSFC will reconnect automatically within 5 minutes. (4) Confirm the witness server can be reached from all cluster nodes: run 'Test-NetConnection -ComputerName <witness_server> -Port 445' from each node."}	null	low	f	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236551
1233	sqlserver	execute	Issue emergency log backup if log space is critically low	{"sql": "-- Replace <database_name> and <backup_path> with actual values\\n-- Only execute if log space > 85% AND recovery model is FULL or BULK_LOGGED\\nBACKUP LOG [<database_name>]\\n  TO DISK = N'<backup_path>\\\\<database_name>_emergency_log.bak'\\n  WITH STATS = 10, COMPRESSION;", "parameters": ["<database_name>: target database name", "<backup_path>: local or UNC path for backup file"], "description": "Take an emergency log backup to free log space while the full/differential backup is still running. SQL Server allows concurrent log backups during active full backups."}	null	low	t	f	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236652
1178	sqlserver	instruct	Implement pre-maintenance quorum safety procedure for future windows	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "To prevent future maintenance windows from exposing the cluster to quorum risk: (1) Before taking the witness offline, temporarily adjust quorum to 'No Majority — Disk only' or suspend automatic quorum management: 'Set-ClusterQuorum -NoWitness' (removes witness vote without removing the witness configuration). (2) Alternatively, use Node Weight adjustment to ensure remaining nodes have sufficient votes: '(Get-ClusterNode \\"<node_name>\\").NodeWeight = 1'. (3) Add a check to the pre-maintenance checklist: confirm cluster can tolerate witness absence before proceeding. (4) After maintenance: restore quorum with 'Set-ClusterQuorum -FileShareWitness \\\\\\\\<witness>\\\\<share>' to re-enable the witness vote."}	null	low	f	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236552
1182	sqlserver	execute	Take an immediate log backup to reclaim freed space	{"sql": "-- Replace <database_name> and <backup_path> with actual values\\nBACKUP LOG [<database_name>]\\n  TO DISK = N'<backup_path>\\\\<database_name>_log_after_kill_'\\n    + REPLACE(CONVERT(NVARCHAR, GETDATE(), 120), ':', '-') + '.bak'\\n  WITH COMPRESSION, STATS = 10;", "parameters": ["database_name: the affected database", "backup_path: valid backup destination path"], "description": "After the transaction is killed and rollback completes, take a log backup to truncate the log and reclaim VLF space. Without this backup, the log file retains its current size even though the blocker is gone."}	null	low	f	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236554
1185	sqlserver	execute	Take an immediate log backup to relieve current log pressure	{"sql": "-- Execute for each affected database\\n-- Replace <database_name> and <backup_path> with actual values\\nBACKUP LOG [<database_name>]\\n  TO DISK = N'<backup_path>\\\\<database_name>_log_emergency_'\\n    + REPLACE(CONVERT(NVARCHAR, GETDATE(), 120), ':', '-') + '.bak'\\n  WITH COMPRESSION,\\n       CHECKSUM,\\n       STATS = 10;", "parameters": ["database_name: name of the affected database", "backup_path: valid UNC path or local path for backup destination"], "description": "Take an immediate log backup to truncate the active log and release VLF space before scheduling long-term frequency improvements."}	null	low	f	t	00:05:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236556
1186	sqlserver	instruct	Create or modify SQL Agent job for frequent log backups	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "Create a SQL Server Agent job to back up transaction logs at the required frequency: (1) In SSMS, expand SQL Server Agent → Jobs → New Job. Name it '<Database>_LogBackup_15min'. (2) Add a job step with T-SQL: 'BACKUP LOG [<database>] TO DISK = N''<path>\\\\<database>_log_'' + REPLACE(CONVERT(NVARCHAR, GETDATE(), 120), '':'', ''-'') + ''.bak'' WITH COMPRESSION, CHECKSUM'. (3) Set the schedule to recur every 15 minutes (or as required by RPO) during business hours; every 30 minutes off-hours. (4) Add notifications: email the DBA team on failure. (5) Alternatively, if using Ola Hallengren's maintenance solution, modify the DatabaseBackup job schedule from hourly to 15-minute intervals for FULL recovery databases."}	null	low	t	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236557
