1271	sqlserver	execute	Back up log and shrink to free active VLF space	{"sql": "-- Step 1: Back up the transaction log to free inactive VLFs\\n-- Replace <DatabaseName> and <BackupPath>\\nBACKUP LOG [<DatabaseName>]\\nTO DISK = N'<BackupPath>\\\\<DatabaseName>_pre_vlf_fix_log.bak'\\nWITH COMPRESSION, STATS = 10;\\n\\n-- Step 2: Shrink the log file (TRUNCATEONLY - does not move data)\\nUSE [<DatabaseName>];\\nDBCC SHRINKFILE (N'<LogFileName>', TRUNCATEONLY);\\n\\n-- Confirm current size after shrink\\nSELECT name, size * 8 / 1024 AS size_mb,\\n  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM sys.dm_db_log_info(DB_ID())) AS vlf_count\\nFROM sys.master_files\\nWHERE database_id = DB_ID() AND type = 1;", "parameters": [], "description": "Back up the transaction log to allow VLF space to be freed, then shrink the log file to its minimum before regrowing to the target size."}	{"sql": "-- If shrink causes issues, regrow log immediately:\\n-- USE [<DatabaseName>];\\n-- ALTER DATABASE [<DatabaseName>] MODIFY FILE (NAME = N'<LogFileName>', SIZE = <OriginalSizeMB>MB);"}	medium	t	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236691
1287	sqlserver	instruct	Grant share and NTFS permissions for SQL Agent service account	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "On the primary server (where backup files are written): (1) Locate the backup share used for log shipping (from backup_directory in log_shipping_primary_databases). (2) Grant the secondary server's SQL Agent service account Read access to the network share (Share Permissions) and NTFS Read permissions on the backup directory. (3) On the secondary server, grant the SQL Agent service account Write access to the copy_destination_directory (local path). (4) If SQL Agent runs as 'NT SERVICE\\\\SQLSERVERAGENT', the machine account (DOMAIN\\\\COMPUTERNAME$) needs the share/NTFS access. (5) Use 'net share' and 'icacls' or Windows Explorer Security tab to verify and set permissions. (6) If a proxy account is used for the LS jobs, update the proxy credential password if it has expired."}	null	medium	t	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236704
1303	sqlserver	instruct	Create or adjust high-frequency log backup job in SQL Server Agent	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["DatabaseName: name of the affected database", "BackupPath: destination folder for log backups (e.g., D:\\\\SQLBackups\\\\LogBackups)", "TIMESTAMP: job token $(ESCAPE_SQUOTE(DATE))_$(ESCAPE_SQUOTE(TIME))"], "description": "In SQL Server Agent, create a new log backup job scheduled to run every 5-15 minutes for the affected databases. Use the following T-SQL template in the job step:\\n\\nBACKUP LOG [$(DatabaseName)]\\n  TO DISK = N'$(BackupPath)\\\\$(DatabaseName)_log_$(TIMESTAMP).bak'\\n  WITH COMPRESSION, STATS = 10;\\n\\nFor each spike-prone database, set the schedule to repeat every 5 minutes during peak hours (or continuously if spikes are unpredictable). Alternatively, use a Maintenance Plan with 'Back Up Database (Log)' task set to every 5 minutes. Ensure the backup destination has sufficient disk space — a 5-minute interval on a high-throughput database can accumulate 288 backup files per day."}	null	low	t	t	00:30:00	2026-02-24 13:10:27.236741
