5794	postgresql	instruct	Recommend sequential key strategy to prevent future fragmentation	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "To prevent recurring index fragmentation from random keys: (1) Replace UUIDv4 with UUIDv7 (time-sortable, RFC 9562) — inserts will be approximately sequential. (2) Alternatively, use BIGSERIAL or IDENTITY columns for primary keys. (3) If UUIDs are required for external compatibility, add a BIGSERIAL surrogate key and create the clustered index on that instead. (4) For existing tables, consider lowering the index fillfactor to 70-80% to absorb random insertions with fewer page splits. (5) Schedule periodic REINDEX CONCURRENTLY (e.g., weekly) until key strategy is changed."}	\N	low	f	t	1-5 days	2026-02-25 08:59:43.77256
