5882	postgresql	instruct	Schedule recurring integrity checks via pg_cron	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "Set up weekly integrity checks: (1) Install pg_cron: CREATE EXTENSION pg_cron; (requires shared_preload_libraries and restart). (2) Schedule weekly check: SELECT cron.schedule('weekly-integrity', '0 2 * * 0', $$ SELECT bt_index_check(c.oid) FROM pg_index i JOIN pg_class c ON c.oid = i.indexrelid WHERE i.indisvalid AND c.relam = (SELECT oid FROM pg_am WHERE amname = ''btree''); $$); (3) Alternative: use OS crontab with pg_amcheck CLI tool. (4) Set up alerting on check failures via log monitoring. (5) For production databases, also enable data_checksums for page-level verification."}	\N	low	f	t	1-5 minutes	2026-02-25 08:59:43.77256
