6659	postgresql	instruct	Configure NUMA-aware PostgreSQL startup and memory allocation	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "System administrator must: (1) Start PostgreSQL with numactl --interleave=all to spread shared memory across NUMA nodes: numactl --interleave=all pg_ctl start. (2) Set vm.zone_reclaim_mode = 0 to prevent premature local memory reclaim. (3) Consider binding PostgreSQL to a single NUMA node if the instance fits: numactl --cpunodebind=0 --membind=0 pg_ctl start. (4) For Linux kernel 3.8+, enable automatic NUMA balancing: echo 1 > /proc/sys/kernel/numa_balancing. (5) Update the PostgreSQL systemd service file to include numactl in ExecStart."}	\N	medium	t	t	5-60 minutes	2026-02-25 08:59:43.77256
