6829	postgresql	instruct	Right-size column definitions and use column order optimization	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "1) Change oversized types: ALTER TABLE t ALTER COLUMN c TYPE varchar(100) (if max actual length is under 100). 2) Replace bigint (8 bytes) with integer (4 bytes) or smallint (2 bytes) where value range permits. 3) Use boolean (1 byte) instead of integer for flags. 4) Reorder columns to minimize alignment padding: put fixed-width columns first (bigint, integer, etc.), then variable-width columns (varchar, text, jsonb) last. 5) Consider normalizing repeated text values into lookup tables."}	\N	medium	t	f	1-5 days	2026-02-25 08:59:43.77256
