8531	postgresql	instruct	Test storage fsync reliability	{"parameters": [], "description": "Test fsync with pg_test_fsync utility (included with PostgreSQL): (1) Run: pg_test_fsync -f /path/to/pgdata/test_fsync. This tests various sync methods and reports throughput. (2) Suspiciously high throughput (>10000 ops/sec on spinning disk) indicates the storage may be caching writes. (3) For definitive testing, use diskchecker.pl from the PostgreSQL wiki which detects data loss during power failures. (4) Known problem devices: consumer SSDs without power-loss protection, USB drives, some NAS appliances, NFS without sync mount option, some virtual disk drivers."}	\N	low	f	t	5-30 minutes	2026-02-25 08:59:43.77256
