8538	postgresql	execute	Repair the corrupted page	{"sql": "-- For index page: REINDEX INDEX CONCURRENTLY :index_name; -- For heap page: if using streaming replication, the page can be restored from a standby: SET zero_damaged_pages = on; SELECT count(*) FROM :table_name; -- Forces read of all pages, zero_damaged_pages replaces corrupt pages with zeros", "parameters": ["index_name", "table_name"], "description": "For index corruption, REINDEX rebuilds cleanly. For heap corruption, options are: (1) Restore the specific table from backup. (2) Use pg_surgery extension (PG 14+) to mark individual tuples. (3) As a last resort, zero_damaged_pages = on skips corrupt pages (causes data loss on that page)."}	\N	medium	t	f	1-5 minutes	2026-02-25 08:59:43.77256
