12635	oracle	instruct	Oracle recommend redo reduction strategies	{"sql": "-- Common redo reduction strategies:\\n-- 1. Batch small updates into larger transactions:\\n--    COMMIT every 1000 rows instead of every row\\n-- 2. Use direct-path INSERT for bulk loads:\\n--    INSERT /*+ APPEND */ INTO target SELECT * FROM source;\\n-- 3. Avoid UPDATE of unchanged columns:\\n--    UPDATE t SET col1=:val WHERE col1 != :val;\\n-- 4. Use MERGE instead of separate INSERT/UPDATE:\\n--    MERGE INTO target USING source ON (...) WHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE...", "parameters": [], "description": "Provides application-level recommendations for reducing redo generation through SQL pattern optimization"}	\N	low	f	t	1-5 minutes	2026-02-28 22:39:08.596677
