13265	oracle	instruct	ora_build_risk_assessment_report	{"sql": "-- Build risk assessment with these dimensions:\\n-- 1. SECURITY RISK (Critical):\\n--    - Number of unfixed CVEs (from Oracle CPU quarterly reports)\\n--    - CVSS scores for applicable vulnerabilities\\n--    - Attack surface (internet-facing? internal only?)\\n--    - Compliance gaps: SOC2/PCI-DSS require supported software\\n\\n-- 2. OPERATIONAL RISK (High):\\n--    - No bug fixes from Oracle (only workarounds)\\n--    - Incompatibility with newer OS versions, drivers, tools\\n--    - Unable to use new Oracle features (performance, security)\\n\\n-- 3. FINANCIAL RISK (Medium):\\n--    - Extended Support premium costs\\n--    - Potential audit findings and penalties\\n--    - Data breach liability (running unpatched software)\\n\\n-- Quantify with Oracle data:\\nSELECT 'Database Size' AS metric, TO_CHAR(SUM(bytes)/1024/1024/1024, '999,999.9') || ' GB' AS value FROM dba_data_files\\nUNION ALL SELECT 'Tables', TO_CHAR(COUNT(*)) FROM dba_tables WHERE owner NOT IN ('SYS','SYSTEM')\\nUNION ALL SELECT 'Active Users', TO_CHAR(COUNT(*)) FROM dba_users WHERE account_status = 'OPEN'\\nUNION ALL SELECT 'Daily Transactions', TO_CHAR(value) FROM v$sysstat WHERE name = 'user commits';", "parameters": [], "description": "Build comprehensive risk assessment report quantifying security, operational, and financial risks"}	\N	low	t	t	hours	2026-02-28 22:39:08.596677
