13298	oracle	instruct	ora_establish_offline_patch_process	{"sql": "-- Establish secure offline patch delivery process:\\n-- 1. PATCH DOWNLOAD (on connected workstation):\\n--    a. Download from Oracle MOS: https://support.oracle.com\\n--    b. Download CPU patch + OPatch update\\n--    c. Verify SHA-256 checksums against MOS published values\\n--    d. Record patch number, description, and prerequisites\\n\\n-- 2. SECURE TRANSFER:\\n--    a. Copy to approved removable media (encrypted USB/DVD)\\n--    b. Transfer through data diode or air-gap bridge\\n--    c. Scan media with approved AV before introducing to secure zone\\n--    d. Verify checksums on target side match source\\n\\n-- 3. PATCH STAGING:\\n--    a. Copy to staging directory on Oracle server\\n--    b. Verify OPatch version compatibility:\\n--       $ORACLE_HOME/OPatch/opatch version\\n--    c. Update OPatch first if required:\\n--       unzip p6880880_*.zip -d $ORACLE_HOME\\n--    d. Run conflict check:\\n--       opatch prereq CheckConflictAgainstOHWithDetail -ph /staging/patch\\n\\n-- 4. DOCUMENTATION:\\n--    Maintain offline patch inventory tracking\\n--    Log all media transfers with chain-of-custody\\nSELECT 'Last Patched' AS metric, TO_CHAR(MAX(action_time), 'YYYY-MM-DD') AS value FROM dba_registry_sqlpatch;", "parameters": [], "description": "Establish secure offline patch delivery and transfer process for air-gapped Oracle environments"}	\N	medium	t	t	hours	2026-02-28 22:39:08.596677
