8114	postgresql	execute	Stop old primary and rewind to new timeline	{"sql": null, "parameters": ["new_primary"], "description": "1) IMMEDIATELY stop the old primary: sudo systemctl stop postgresql (on the old primary node). 2) If data reconciliation needed, export divergent data first: pg_dump -h old_primary > divergent_data.sql. 3) pg_rewind: pg_rewind --target-pgdata=/var/lib/postgresql/data --source-server='host=:new_primary port=5432 user=replication'. 4) Create standby.signal. 5) Set primary_conninfo pointing to new primary. 6) Set recovery_target_timeline='latest'. 7) Start as standby: sudo systemctl start postgresql."}	\N	medium	t	f	minutes	2026-02-25 08:59:43.77256
