10012	postgresql	instruct	Address recovery stall or accelerate recovery	{"description": "If recovery is stalled:\\n1. Check disk space: df -h /var/lib/postgresql\\n2. Check WAL availability: ls -la pg_wal/\\n3. Check for recovery.conf or standby.signal issues\\n4. Verify primary is accessible for WAL streaming\\n\\nTo accelerate recovery:\\n1. Increase max_wal_size on primary to prevent WAL recycling\\n2. Increase wal_keep_size to retain more WAL segments\\n3. Set recovery_target_timeline = 'latest' if stuck on wrong timeline\\n4. If replica, consider pg_basebackup to start fresh if lag is too large\\n\\nFor crash recovery on primary:\\n1. Ensure sufficient disk space for WAL replay\\n2. Check pg_xlog/pg_wal for corrupted segments\\n3. Consider pg_resetwal only as absolute last resort (data loss risk)"}	\N	medium	t	f	Variable	2026-02-25 08:59:43.77256
