10662	postgresql	instruct	Implement OS-level egress firewall rules	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "Configure OS-level outbound firewall rules: (1) For iptables: iptables -A OUTPUT -m owner --uid-owner postgres -j DROP (default deny for postgres user). (2) Then allow specific destinations: iptables -I OUTPUT -m owner --uid-owner postgres -d <backup_server_ip> -j ACCEPT. (3) Allow DNS resolution: iptables -I OUTPUT -m owner --uid-owner postgres -p udp --dport 53 -j ACCEPT. (4) Allow NTP: iptables -I OUTPUT -m owner --uid-owner postgres -p udp --dport 123 -j ACCEPT. (5) Save rules: iptables-save > /etc/iptables.rules. (6) For firewalld: use direct rules or rich rules targeting the postgres user."}	\N	medium	t	t	15-30 minutes	2026-02-25 08:59:43.77256
