10701	postgresql	instruct	Plan logical replication-based minimal-downtime upgrade	{"sql": null, "parameters": [], "description": "Minimal-downtime upgrade plan: (1) Set wal_level = 'logical' on old server if not already set (requires restart). (2) Install target PostgreSQL version on new hardware/VM. (3) Create schema on new server using pg_dump --schema-only. (4) Create rootcauseations on old server: CREATE rootcauseATION upgrade_pub FOR ALL TABLES. (5) Create subscriptions on new server: CREATE SUBSCRIPTION upgrade_sub CONNECTION 'host=old_host dbname=...' rootcauseATION upgrade_pub. (6) Wait for initial sync to complete (monitor pg_stat_subscription). (7) During maintenance window: stop writes, wait for replication to catch up, switch application connections to new server. (8) Drop subscription and rootcauseation after validation."}	\N	medium	t	t	15-30 minutes	2026-02-25 08:59:43.77256
