35670	mariadb	recommendation	Resolve PRI-001-RC15 (mysql)	{"action": "Cached or active-transaction queries reference PII columns. Actions: (1) review the rows — each links a session/transaction/query_text to a sensitive table and column; (2) for cached_plan rows, identify the application or job that produced the query and verify legitimate business need; (3) for active_transaction rows, investigate why a session is holding state on PII data — if unintentional, terminate; (4) enforce column-level access controls and dynamic data masking; (5) ensure DAM logging captures access to sensitive tables."}	\N	critical	f	t	\N	2026-05-11 22:17:39.229791
35671	mariadb	immediate	AUD-015-RC01: Triage schema and DML events from mysql.general_log - MySQL	{"action": "Query events: SELECT event_time, SUBSTRING_INDEX(user_host,'@',1) AS login, argument AS statement FROM mysql.general_log WHERE event_time >= NOW() - INTERVAL 1 DAY AND command_type = 'Query' AND argument REGEXP '^[[:space:]]*(CREATE|ALTER|DROP|INSERT|UPDATE|DELETE|TRUNCATE)[[:space:]]' ORDER BY event_time DESC LIMIT 5000. For each row: verify the login against the list of authorized application and deployer accounts (SELECT user FROM mysql.user WHERE Select_priv = 'Y'). Flag any statement issued by an application account that performed DDL (CREATE/ALTER/DROP) outside a maintenance window. Record the statement and user_host for all unauthorized events."}	\N	medium	f	f	\N	2026-05-11 22:17:39.229791
35672	mariadb	configure	AUD-015-RC01: Revoke DDL grants from application accounts and enable periodic review - MySQL	{"action": "Revoke DDL privileges from application service accounts: REVOKE CREATE, ALTER, DROP ON <db>.* FROM '<app_user>'@'%'. Create a deployer account with DDL rights: CREATE USER 'deployer'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY '<strong_password>'; GRANT CREATE, ALTER, DROP ON <db>.* TO 'deployer'@'localhost'. Confirm privileges: SHOW GRANTS FOR '<app_user>'@'%'. Schedule a daily MySQL Event to summarize schema changes from general_log and write to a review table: CREATE EVENT aud015_daily_review ON SCHEDULE EVERY 1 DAY DO INSERT INTO <schema>.schema_change_review SELECT ... FROM mysql.general_log WHERE argument REGEXP 'CREATE|ALTER|DROP' AND event_time >= NOW() - INTERVAL 1 DAY. Ensure general_log is kept enabled: SET GLOBAL general_log = ON."}	\N	low	f	t	\N	2026-05-11 22:17:39.229791
